{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'D382|D384|D490' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"4107:## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n4116:  a related thesis opens; what the closing check rejects is still dropped, including the cash flow he ruled out. Amends D209 beyond D382.\n4119:## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\n4124:  out under D382. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §36.\n5553:    articles (D382, D384); 145 kept statements of the company's own figures have no question. Production lacks the supply commitments (its\n5567:- **To Alex (his D382 and D384; nothing is sent before he answers):** (1) test questions on the company's main numbers on the new system\n5571:## D490 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a test: the new system may open questions on the company's revenue and margin\n5573:- **Asked** (after D489, his reply to this exact question): \"这一周的对比显示：现行系统会为营收、毛利率开问题；新系统按你之前定的规则（D382：财务数字是条件，不是\n5577:  新鲜周。会改变你的 D382/D384。历史上类似的放开曾多开 7 个不该开的问题（那次同时改了三处）。\"\n5579:  request until a result is adopted). D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path; the arm departs from them on one point, the\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/audit-c20-blind.md; cat docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/PROBE-DESIGN.md'","aggregated_output":"**The candidate reflects the signed standard’s main-driver category, but it is wider than the test Alex approved in D490, and it leaves two practical gaps: how to avoid duplicate questions and how to give an annual question a supported release date.** For example, “an airline’s fuel cost” is a valid example in the signed standard, but D490 asked about testing the company’s revenue and margin; the candidate also invites that fuel-cost question.\n\nThis is a read-only assessment of the text. It identifies possible model behavior, not measured results. I compared the system and closing files with `diff` and compared the schemas as parsed JSON. The schema changes only the reason description from four to five and adds `main_driver` to the enum.\n\n### Each changed sentence\n\nSources: [candidate system](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt:87), [candidate closing check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt:14), [candidate schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json:49), [signed standard](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:272), and [D490](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5571).\n\n| Change | Verdict | Source and reasoning |\n|---|---|---|\n| “It opens for one of **five** reasons, a closed set…” | **Consistent with the standard and D490’s test**, conditional on the fifth reason being scoped correctly. | §3 says “开题理由是封闭的” and lists five categories. D490 opens a test departure from D382/D384; those decisions still govern the adopted request. |\n| “**main_driver: the annual quantity that carries the company’s value, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company guides it**…” | **Consistent with §3; keeps wider than D490’s stated test.** | Row A says “承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引” and “公司财年的今年或明年.” D490’s exact question was how to handle “营收和毛利率,” and the approved option was to test questions of that kind. “Annual quantity” also permits other measures. D490’s later summary says “company’s main numbers,” so the record itself is broader than its exact question; that breadth should not silently expand the test. |\n| “…**the revenue of the segment that carries the business, or the gross margin**…” | **Consistent**, subject to the separate-bet test. | Row A expressly names “撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率.” Section 4 adds “一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开” and requires independently different business outcomes. A major segment is not automatically a second question beside total revenue. |\n| “**the bank’s net interest income this fiscal year; the retailer’s same-store sales growth next fiscal year; an airline’s fuel cost only when it is the focus of debate**” | **Consistent with the standard in substance; keeps wider than D490’s test.** | Row A names bank net interest income, retailer same-store sales and airline fuel cost when debated. The standard says same-store sales; the example specifies **growth**, which can describe the same outcome in another form and needs the duplicate check. Fuel cost and potentially same-store sales are outside the clearly stated revenue-and-margin test. |\n| “**It is not every line of the statements.**” | **Consistent.** | Row A: “不是每一行报表数.” Section 4 also rejects opening every line of guidance. |\n| “**The material that publishes the figure settles it, usually the annual report, on its release date.**” | **Consistent, but incomplete as an instruction for an unknown date.** | Row A: “公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报”; “到期日是这个数的发布日.” The sentence identifies the kind of date but does not explain what to return when the item does not supply the release day. |\n| Revised do-not-open row: “**a quarter’s figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own**” | **Consistent with §3–4 as a general main-driver exception; keeps wider than D490’s stated test.** | §4 excludes “季度数字和季度指引” and every line of the same guidance; row A permits a qualifying annual main driver. Since `main_driver` is wider than revenue and margin, the exception is wider too. The qualifying “on its own” also leaves other opening reasons available, which is appropriate. |\n| Closing check: “**five reasons**” instead of four | **Consistent as bookkeeping; inherits the wider fifth reason.** | §3 has five categories; D490 permits the test exception. The remaining checks still require a public settlement, separate outcome and compliance with the do-not-open list. |\n| Schema description “**one of the five**” and enum addition `main_driver` | **Consistent as representation; inherits the same scope issue.** | Row A names `main_driver`. The enum makes the new answer expressible; it does not itself limit which measures qualify. |\n\nD382 says financial figures are conditions unless there is a reason that is the view; D384 excludes class A from the adopted clean path. D490 authorizes **testing** an exception, not adoption of the candidate. [D382 and D384](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4107).\n\n### Conflicts and tensions inside the request\n\n- **Role paragraph:** No direct contradiction. A main annual question can be an important question raised by an item, supported by evidence. “Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home” still rules out opening one merely because a figure appears.\n- **CONDITION:** No direct contradiction. A financial figure can be recorded as a condition and inform a revenue or earnings question; the fifth reason can also allow a qualifying annual question. The wording about an **open** thesis does not prohibit a new one: the next sentence explicitly says “open or new.”\n- **One quantity, one period:** No direct contradiction, but the growth example exposes an ambiguity. A level and its growth may be two ways to ask about the same result, rather than two separately bettable outcomes.\n- **Date rule:** There is a real instruction gap. The new reason says the figure’s release date settles it, but the general date paragraph does not list `main_driver` among the reasons whose date it fixes. It starts “Give the date the item supports” and ends by rejecting a question no date can settle. An item may identify FY revenue without giving its publication day; the schema does not supply that day.\n- **Another estimate, source or wording:** Compatible in principle. It prevents a revised forecast or another phrasing of an already tracked result from becoming another question. It does not explicitly show that **level versus growth** can be the same underlying result.\n- **Annual quantity after next year:** Compatible with “current or next fiscal year.” Both reject an annual main-driver question beyond that window. The request should not reinterpret a later-year forecast as a current-year forecast.\n- **`closest_open_thesis` and `why_a_separate_bet`:** Compatible and useful for an existing question. They require a reason the answers can move apart. They do not explicitly require the same independent-bet comparison **between two new questions**: the closing check checks same underlying question among new proposals, but its “cannot move apart” test names only an open thesis.\n- **Closing check on figures and conditions:** The instruction not to drop a reported figure merely because it was retold concerns *evidence*, not automatic question opening. The same-fact row combines a reported measure and its growth in one evidence item; it does not decide whether two research questions are independently meaningful. The final cash-flow check applies only to **unlinked company figures**; a figure linked to a newly opened question does not receive that particular check. The earlier general evidence test still applies. This makes the decision to open a question consequential for what survives.\n- **Closing check on reasons:** Changing four to five is internally consistent. It does not say that the new fifth reason replaces the other four.\n\n### Examples\n\nThe new examples use generic bank, retailer and airline descriptions. They name no covered company, product or number, and draw on several industries. Their measures are supported by row A, with the qualification that the retailer example changes “same-store sales” to “same-store sales **growth**.”\n\nThey fit the schema’s ability to express a question, outcome, period, reason and settling material, but **the examples themselves do not supply a release date or identify the public document**. They are measure examples, not complete valid output examples. The airline example agrees with the standard but exceeds the clearly stated revenue-and-margin test.\n\n### Specific risks and smallest wording changes\n\nThese are risks in how the request can be read, not claims that the model will make these mistakes.\n\n**(a) Every statement line, including EPS, net income, cash flow or a small segment.** The limiting words are “the annual quantity that carries the company’s value,” “not every line” and “only matters an analyst would bet on separately.” They make indiscriminate opening contrary to the text, but “annual quantity” leaves the model to decide whether any of those measures carries value. The fuel-cost example makes the category visibly broader than revenue and margin.\n\nFor the D490 test, the smallest scope correction is to replace **“the annual quantity”** with **“the company’s annual revenue or margin”**, and remove or replace examples outside that scope. Retain the existing importance and separate-bet tests. This is a restriction to the approved test, not a claim that the signed standard excludes other main drivers.\n\n**(b) A quarter or a year after next fiscal year.** The explicit “current or next fiscal year,” quarter exclusion and “annual quantity after next year” oppose both. No additional prohibition is needed. A missing fiscal year is a separate problem: the model should not infer one from a quarterly figure or a distant forecast.\n\n**(c) Two questions for level and growth, or total and main segment.** “Same-store sales growth” alongside “revenue” and “gross margin,” combined with “one quantity,” can make the same result look like two different measures. A main segment is explicitly eligible, while the separate-bet check against **new** questions is less explicit than against open ones.\n\nThe smallest sourced clarification is: **“Compare each proposed question with open and other proposed questions: if the same result settles both, keep one; separate them only if their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on them separately.”** This follows §4’s “同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题” and its separate-bet test. It does **not** categorically merge total and segment: §4 says to judge the actual material, and a segment can have independent drivers.\n\n**(d) Another company’s figures.** For this new reason, “the company” is defined as `current_entity`, and “the company’s value” points back to it. The condition field also excludes other companies’ figures. Those words constrain the new category; an inadvertent opening remains possible because evidence can describe another party, but the candidate does not instruct it. A minimal clarification, if needed, is **“the current entity’s own annual revenue or margin.”** Note that the signed standard separately permits proposing another company’s own question subject to its tests; this candidate’s current-entity scope is narrower, so do not generalize this restriction beyond the requested test.\n\n**(e) The other four reasons stop opening.** There is no explicit instruction to stop them: the five reasons are alternatives and all four remain in the schema. The broad financial prohibition applies to a financial measure **on its own**, while the other categories have their own criteria. A model could nevertheless overapply that row to an obligation or shared quantity. The smallest clarification is **“This financial-figure row does not exclude a matter that independently meets another reason.”** That restates the existing closed-set structure rather than adding a new opening reason.\n\n### What is missing to write the question\n\n- **Measure and scope:** The schema has `description` and `outcome`, but neither explicitly asks for the exact measure and scope—such as total revenue versus a named segment, or which margin. Section 4 requires “算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚.” The answer can express this, but the new instruction does not make the distinction explicit.\n- **Fiscal year:** The new reason requires current or next fiscal year, and `period` can carry it. It does not tell the model what to do if the source does not identify a supported fiscal year. Section 4 requires the subject, measure and time to be supported by the source; it should not invent one.\n- **Settling material:** Present: `settled_by` requires public material, and the new sentence says the publication of the figure, usually the annual report. The document should actually publish the specified measure and scope.\n- **Date:** The *kind* of date is present—the figure’s release date—but a supported actual day may be absent. The schema’s `period` allows null and combines period with check date; `settled_by` is only a string. The request does not resolve how to supply an unknown future release date without inventing it. Section 4 requires a date and public material, and permits an analyst-set date only in the specified cases; it does not provide that fallback for the annual main driver.# Can the new system open questions on the company's revenue and margin without number cards? Probe design, version 2 (D490), 2026-11-14\n\n**What it can decide.** Whether c20, the adopted clean Step 1 request (c8) with one more reason in its closed set (the company's own annual\nrevenue or gross margin), opens the three questions the fresh week showed it lacks (fiscal 2027 revenue, fiscal 2028 revenue, the fiscal\n2028 gross margin) on the stored articles that carry them, keeps and links the figures those articles state, opens no question on other\nstatement lines, quarters or other companies' figures, and does not suppress what c8 opens today. Two steps: step one on the stored\nstates; step two, only after step one passes, the same later articles against a state that already holds the new questions (does it open\nthem twice, or file a year under the wrong year?). Both must pass before the forward draw on the second fresh week. A failure stops the line\nand goes to Alex. Neither step shows how one article's choices shape the next over a week (only a forward draw does), nor whether final\njudgements improve.\n\n**Alex's word (D490):** \"试开这类问题\", on the option \"先在这周已存的文章上…试：能否开出这 3 个问题，同时不乱开、不重复；通过后再跑第二个没用过的新鲜周\". D382 and D384\nstay in force for the adopted path; the arm departs from them on this one point, for the test.\n\n## The candidate (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-*`)\n\nOne direction, stated at its owners (the differences from c8, all of them):\n- **§3's closed set gains a fifth reason, first in the list:** \"main_driver: the company's own annual revenue or gross margin, for its\n  current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company guides it: the revenue that carries the business, in total or of its main segment,\n  or the gross margin (\"the bank's net interest income this fiscal year\"; \"the retailer's same-store sales next fiscal year\"). It is not\n  every line of the statements. Name the measure, its scope and the fiscal year; a level and its growth rate are one thesis when the same\n  reported figure settles both. The material that publishes the figure, usually the annual report, settles it.\"\n- **The date rule** gains \"a main_driver quantity, the release of that fiscal year's results\" among the dates a reason fixes when the item\n  gives none.\n- **The do-not-open row** \"a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period, on its own\" becomes \"a quarter's figures\n  or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own\".\n- \"four reasons\" becomes \"five reasons\" in §3 and in the closing check; the schema's `opens_as` gains `main_driver` and its description says\n  five.\n- Nothing else changes: the CONDITION bullet already sends the company's figures to \"an open thesis about its revenue or earnings path\"\n  (\"open or new\" in its next sentence); \"another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks\" and \"an annual quantity after\n  next year\" stand; `closest_open_thesis` and `why_a_separate_bet` are as they were.\n\n**Source.** The signed standard §3, row A: \"A 主驱动量 | main_driver | 标的 | 承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息\n收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数 | 量，五档 | 公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日 | 公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报\";\n§4 for the quarter row (\"季度数字和季度指引\"), for writing who and what is counted (\"算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚\") and for one result settling one\nquestion (\"同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题\"). The two examples are the row's own; none names the covered company, a product or a number.\n\n**Narrower than row A, on purpose, by D490's scope.** The row is \"the annual quantity that carries the company's value\" and also names\ncapital expenditure, a utility's rate base and an airline's fuel cost; Alex opened the test for revenue and margin, so the arm says revenue\nor gross margin and carries only the two revenue examples. A question on another annual quantity is therefore outside the request as\nwritten and counts as a number card below; that is a limit of this test, not a reading of the standard, and the frozen standard is not\nchanged. If the arm is ever adopted, the narrowing goes to Alex.\n\n**Size.** System text 15,828 → 16,556 characters (+728); closing check the same length; schema one enum value. Growth reason: the standard's\nrow A has no sentence in the request (left out by D384); D490 opens the test of carrying it; no sentence can be cut for it without becoming\na second direction.\n\n**Reviews before any send.** Blind audit of version 1 (`audit-c20-blind.md`): wider than D490 (fixed: revenue or gross margin), no date for\nan item that gives none (fixed: the date rule), a growth example that reads as a second measure (fixed: the example and the level-and-growth\nsentence), measure and scope not asked for (fixed). Council round 13 (`mw-codex-13.md`): the counting below. A synthetic answer following the\narm (one main_driver thesis, one linked statement) passes the arm's schema and every runner check; the same answer fails c8's schema and a\nreason outside the set fails the arm's, as they must.\n\n**Prompt audit row** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit`, §3):\n\n| Failure class | The request's sentences | The standard's line | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| The company's revenue and margin are never questions: 3 of the 5 matters both reader families listed; the stored reasoning names the sentence at 109 of 235 steps; 145 kept figure statements have no question | \"It opens for one of four reasons, a closed set\"; \"Do not open a thesis about: … a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period, on its own\" | §3 row A | The request removes what the standard keeps, by Alex's D382 and D384; not a model misread. D490 opens the test of carrying the row for revenue and margin. |\n\n**What arm c1 teaches (`LOG.md` §20).** c1's \"a measure with a reason the item supports is a view\" let any conditional count as a reason\n(7 unwanted theses in 48 sends) and its narrower link sentence left a margin figure outside the revenue view, with three levers in one arm.\nc20 has no \"reason\" clause and touches no link sentence; the links are counted below because c1 failed there.\n\n## Step one: the stored states\n\nThe reviewed probe (`clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/identity-probe/probe_identity.py`) unchanged: it first rebuilds every stored\nrequest byte for byte, then replaces only the three arm files. Both arms on all ten cases, three sends each: **60 sends**; about $0.55 at the\nweek's mean call cost ($0.0089) and $0.86 at the script's estimate (9,500 output tokens a call); spending ceiling $2.00. (Claude told Alex\n\"a few cents\"; the honest figure for both steps is about one dollar. The step's spend so far is $4.69.)\n\nCases (`cases-main-numbers.json`; the stored week's own c8 requests and before-states, none of which holds a revenue or margin question):\n\n| case | step | what the article holds | matters it should open | facts that must be kept and linked there |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| t1-target | 11 | consensus only | FY2027 revenue, FY2028 revenue | the $406.05 billion and $671.95 billion sales estimates |\n| t2-target | 16 | the 70% outlook against the 45% modelled; margin estimates under 72% by the fourth quarter | FY2028 revenue | the 70% outlook |\n| t4-target | 121 | the fiscal-2027 consensus; the 70% outlook; margins 72%–73% in fiscal 2028 | FY2027 revenue, FY2028 revenue, FY2028 gross margin | the $412 billion consensus; the 70% outlook; the 72%–73% outlook |\n| t5-target | 98 | the 70% outlook; the 72%–73% margin outlook against a consensus of steady margins | FY2028 revenue, FY2028 gross margin | the 70% outlook; the 72%–73% outlook |\n| t6-target | 92 | the fiscal-2027 consensus; the 70% outlook; AMD's and Broadcom's figures | FY2027 revenue, FY2028 revenue | the $406.05 billion consensus; the 70% outlook |\n| g1-guard | 13 | only last quarter's reported figure ($89 billion of data-center revenue) | reported only | |\n| g2-guard | 37 | EPS forecasts for two fiscal years, net income, the third-quarter guide | none on EPS, net income or a quarter | |\n| g3-guard | 5 | AMD's revenue and guidance beside NVIDIA's profit | none on another company's figure | |\n| k1-keep | 14 | c8 opened the supply-commitments thesis here (stored draw) | | |\n| k2-keep | 35 | c8 opened the Vera Rubin thesis here; the quarter's results and the third-quarter guide are in the article | | |\n\n**Who reads.** Claude reads every answer, send by send, beside the article, and keeps the listing. Because the author must not grade the\nchange alone (AGENTS §7.1), two blind reader families (Codex, a Claude subagent) get every new thesis of both arms with its article, the\narms under shuffled labels, and mark by what the question asks, whatever its reason label: the company's revenue or gross margin for fiscal\n2027 or 2028 (with measure, scope and year) / another statement line / a quarter / a later year / another company's figure / not a figure\nquestion; and, for two new theses in one answer, whether the same reported result settles both. Where the readers and Claude differ, the\nitem is listed with each reading and counted as the readers have it when they agree.\n\n**Counting** (frozen before any send; fractions are of valid sends, a valid send being one whose answer passed the checks):\n- *Valid sends:* at least two of three per case and arm, or that case is inconclusive for that arm (listed).\n- *A main-number thesis for a matter:* a new thesis asking the company's revenue (total or its main segment) or gross margin for that fiscal\n  year, naming measure, scope and year. A growth-rate question counts for that year's revenue only when it names the measure, the scope and\n  the year it grows over, so that the year's reported revenue settles it; otherwise it is listed as unclear and not counted. Level or growth,\n  total or segment: the shape is reported for every thesis.\n- **Opened:** each of the three matters is opened in at least two thirds of c20's valid sends on at least half of the cases listed for it\n  (FY2027 revenue: t1, t4, t6; FY2028 revenue: t1, t2, t4, t5, t6; FY2028 gross margin: t4 and t5, both needed). *No room:* c8 opens a\n  matter in two thirds of its sends on any case (it cannot: its schema has no such reason and its row forbids it; listed if it does under\n  another label).\n- **Kept and linked:** for each named fact of a target case, c20 keeps it in no fewer valid sends than c8 less one; and in the sends where\n  c20 opens that fact's matter, the fact is linked to that thesis in at least two thirds of them. A fact neither arm keeps in any send is\n  \"not exercised\" and listed.\n- **Number card (fails):** by what the question asks, on all ten cases: a new c20 thesis on EPS, net income, cash flow, cash, a small\n  segment, the company's capital expenditure, a quarter, a year after fiscal 2028, or another company's figure, where c8 opens the same in\n  at most one send of that case. Fails when it holds in two of three sends of any one case, or in more than three of c20's thirty sends.\n- **Twice in one answer (fails):** two new c20 theses that both reader families say the same reported result settles (a level and its\n  growth for the same measure, scope and year). Same thresholds. A total and its main segment in one answer is listed with both families'\n  marks and fails only when both call it one result.\n- **Suppression (fails):** on k1 or k2, c20 opens the stored thesis (supply commitments; Vera Rubin) in fewer valid sends than c8 by two or\n  more in one case, or by three or more over both. A keep case where c8 itself opens it in fewer than two valid sends is \"control absent,\n  cannot judge\"; with both absent, suppression is not exercised and step one cannot pass. On every case, any other thesis c8 opens in at\n  least two sends and c20 in none is listed and counts as suppression too.\n- *Reported, not lines:* g1, shown with the question and the article (a main-number thesis from a bare reported figure: row A allows it\n  \"whether or not the company guides it\"; it is also the \"喊出来的数字\" Alex ruled out in D382, so it is his to see, not a pass by the standard);\n  every other new thesis of either arm; kept and unlinked counts per arm; each thesis's period and `settled_by`.\n\n**Verdict of step one:** inconclusive = a required case below its valid sends, or suppression not exercised; pass = opened, kept and linked,\nno number card, none twice in one answer, no suppression; fail = anything else.\n\n## Step two (only after step one passes): the same matters met again\n\n- **State, labelled as constructed:** each case's stored before-state plus the three main-number theses in the wording c20 gave most often\n  in step one (FY2027 revenue, FY2028 revenue, FY2028 gross margin), given the next clean ids. The requests are built by the reviewed builder\n  (`identity-probe/build_fresh_trace.py`, which first rebuilds a stored request byte for byte) and sent by the same probe, c20 only (c8\n  cannot hold these theses). Cases: steps 16, 92, 98 and 121 (t2, t6, t5, t4), three sends each: 12 sends, about $0.15.\n- **Opened again (fails):** a new thesis on a measure, scope and fiscal year the state already holds, in two of three sends of any case, or\n  in more than one of the twelve.\n- **Wrong year (fails):** a named fact linked to the thesis of another fiscal year and not to its own, in two of three sends of any case\n  (the 70% outlook under fiscal 2027; the $412 billion consensus under fiscal 2028).\n- **Filed:** each named fact is kept and linked to the open thesis of its measure and year in at least two thirds of valid sends on at\n  least half of its cases.\n- *Reported:* a new thesis on a year or measure the state lacks (the fiscal 2027 gross margin at step 16), with both reader families' marks.\n- **Verdict of step two:** pass = none opened again, no wrong year, filed; anything else, or a case below two valid sends, is not a pass.\n  Without a pass there is no fresh week.\n\n**Stop.** A fail or an inconclusive result at either step stops the line and goes to Alex with the listing (D355); nothing is tuned on\nthese cases, and a change after reading them is a new arm with its own council round.\n\n**After both pass (not part of this probe):** the forward draw on the second fresh week (2026-09-29..10-05) is designed then, with its\nbudget put to Alex first (about $2.50 for the new system alone would take the step slightly past the $8 it was sized at), and with the\nanswer-options step checked for the fifth reason before any send (its code reads `opens_as` for obligations only; its request names no\nclosed set).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'diff -u clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt; diff -u clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-closing.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt'","aggregated_output":"--- clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-system.txt\t2026-11-08 11:02:42\n+++ clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt\t2026-11-14 17:54:56\n@@ -86,8 +86,13 @@\n \n A thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the\n company's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a\n-date; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of four reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\n+date; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of five reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\n evidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:\n+- main_driver: the company's own annual revenue or gross margin, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company\n+  guides it: the revenue that carries the business, in total or of its main segment, or the gross margin (\"the bank's net interest\n+  income this fiscal year\"; \"the retailer's same-store sales next fiscal year\"). It is not every line of the statements. Name the\n+  measure, its scope and the fiscal year; a level and its growth rate are one thesis when the same reported figure settles both.\n+  The material that publishes the figure, usually the annual report, settles it.\n - product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,\n   usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's\n   trial result and its approval) are separate theses (\"will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?\";\n@@ -111,11 +116,11 @@\n   credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n - Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n   undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n-  decision, the current fiscal year-end. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n+  decision, the current fiscal year-end; a main_driver quantity, the release of that fiscal year's results. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n   checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n - Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n-  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a financial measure's level, growth, margin or guidance for any period,\n-  on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n+  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a quarter's figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a\n+  financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n   product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n   obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n   inform, or left unlinked.\n--- clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c8-closing.txt\t2026-11-08 11:01:52\n+++ clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt\t2026-11-14 17:50:12\n@@ -12,5 +12,5 @@\n A report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\n Return only the evidence items you keep.\n Then check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\n-For each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the four reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n+For each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the five reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n An item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,difflib,pathlib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms\\\"); a=json.dumps(json.loads((p/\\\"c8-schema.json\\\").read_text()),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False).splitlines(); b=json.dumps(json.loads((p/\\\"c20-schema.json\\\").read_text()),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False).splitlines(); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,fromfile=\\\"c8-schema parsed\\\",tofile=\\\"c20-schema parsed\\\",lineterm=\\\"\\\")))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c 'import json,difflib,pathlib; p=pathlib.Path(\\\"clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms\\\"); a=json.dumps(json.loads((p/\\\"c8-schema.json\\\").read_text()),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False).splitlines(); b=json.dumps(json.loads((p/\\\"c20-schema.json\\\").read_text()),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False).splitlines(); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(difflib.unified_diff(a,b,fromfile=\\\"c8-schema parsed\\\",tofile=\\\"c20-schema parsed\\\",lineterm=\\\"\\\")))'\"","aggregated_output":"--- c8-schema parsed\n+++ c20-schema parsed\n@@ -49,12 +49,13 @@\n           \"opens_as\": {\n             \"type\": \"string\",\n             \"enum\": [\n+              \"main_driver\",\n               \"product_node\",\n               \"binding_obligation\",\n               \"shared_quantity\",\n               \"policy_stage\"\n             ],\n-            \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the four in section 3.\"\n+            \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the five in section 3.\"\n           },\n           \"settled_by\": {\n             \"type\": \"string\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
