{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '250,420p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json'","aggregated_output":"ROLE\n\nYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst reading one source item for the company in scope (current_entity); \"the company\" below is that\ncompany. The research already tracked for it is listed in open_theses. Your first job is evidence: decide by the rules below which\nstatements in the item are material, then link each one to every thesis it informs: an open thesis that covers it, a new thesis you\npropose, or both. Your second job is new theses: the important research questions this item raises that no open thesis\ncovers. Every new thesis comes with evidence from this item. A material statement that no open thesis covers and that is not\nitself a big matter (section 3) is returned with empty links: code keeps it in the company's record without links and links it\nwhen a thesis that covers it opens. Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home.\n\nINPUT\n\n- current_entity and company_tags: the company in scope and the companies the item is tagged with. Code assigns the entity; do not\n  invent one. Evidence can describe another party when it informs research on the company.\n- open_theses: the identity, question, tracked outcome and period of each thesis already tracked. They tell you where evidence belongs\n  and whether an idea is already covered; they are not evidence. You do not see the evidence already stored; a later step compares\n  new evidence with history.\n- source_item: the complete text and its source metadata.\n\n1. EVIDENCE: WHAT TO KEEP\n\n- A material statement is one of four kinds. (1) The company's own figure, guidance or decision: \"same-store sales rose 4.2% in the\n  quarter\"; \"management guided full-year revenue to $12–13 billion\"; \"the board approved a $10 billion buyback\". (2) A customer's,\n  supplier's, competitor's or partner's action or reported figure with a size, date or name that bears on the company's demand,\n  supply, input costs, competition, prices or products: \"the largest customer said it will cut orders by a fifth next year\"; \"a bank\n  chose a rival's system\"; \"a software firm is integrating the company's model into its government systems\"; \"the main supplier said\n  its capacity will double by 2027\"; \"a rival cut list prices 15% in Europe\"; \"the largest customer reported its order backlog doubled\n  to $40 billion\". An action is a step the item reports as news: taken, decided or planned (an order, a contract, a selection, an\n  integration under way, an expansion, a cut, a price change, a deployment plan). A party that already uses, hosts, runs or has built\n  on the company's products, and the benefits it describes from that use (faster, cheaper, more accurate), describe an arrangement in\n  place, which is background; its own revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amounts are figures under (2) (\"a hospital chain uses\n  the company's scheduling software and reports shorter waits\"). (3) A named party's new claim or estimate about the company or its\n  industry, with or without a figure, whether an analyst, a customer's or rival's executive or an official makes it: \"the CFO said\n  plants built a decade ago still run at full capacity\"; \"an analyst raised next year's EPS estimate to $4.10\"; \"an analyst said the\n  bank's loan losses next quarter will come in well above consensus\"; \"a short seller accused the company of overstating receivables\n  by $2 billion\". (4) A policy or regulatory decision or\n  step, including one still in force that the item reports: \"the regulator approved the drug for a second indication\"; \"the\n  government required licences for exports of the product\"; \"the regulator still bars sales of the drug in the country\".\n- Go through the item from its first paragraph to its last, including paragraphs about matters other than the headline. The four\n  kinds describe what material statements usually look like; they do not decide what is kept. Take a statement when an analyst\n  following the company would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, and no row\n  of the closing check at the end of this request rejects it; a row's \"it does not cover\" clause sends the statement back to that test\n  and keeps it only where the row says so. Most of an item is background, but a page with eight statements that pass yields eight\n  evidence items, not a selection.\n\n2. LINK EACH STATEMENT TO ITS THESES\n\n- EXISTING: if an open thesis covers the statement, link it to that thesis's exact supplied ID, including contrary facts. Do not\n  return or rename the thesis's description.\n- NEW: if the statement raises a research question that merits separate tracking and no open or newly proposed thesis covers it,\n  propose a thesis (section 3) and link the statement to it.\n- NO THESIS YET: if no open or newly proposed thesis covers a statement you judge material, and the matter is not big enough by\n  its own scale to merit a thesis (section 3), return it with empty links; it is kept without links.\n- CONDITION: a statement of the company's own financial figures (a reported result or balance, its guidance, or a named party's\n  or consensus estimate) lists its useful figures in figures. Its results, guidance and estimates, margins included, inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings\n  path when they bear on that path; a different period is not on its own a reason to leave them unlinked. When no open or new\n  thesis covers it, its links stay empty. A figure is useful when it can change what an analyst\n  expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position: a retailer's quarterly\n  same-store sales, an airline's guidance for next year's unit costs and analysts' consensus earnings for a bank are; a cash-rich\n  company's cash balance or cash flow usually changes none of these when the item ties it to nothing, while a heavily indebted\n  firm's cash burn changes its credit risk. The share price, a target price and other companies' figures are never conditions.\n- Link one statement to every thesis it informs, and to none that its own relevance says it does not inform; use the narrowest\n  relevant thesis only when choosing between theses that cover the same thing.\n- Match by the underlying question or outcome, subject and scope, and time when relevant, not by word overlap. A different wording,\n  source, forecast or direction alone does not make a new thesis. Related questions can be separate when their outcomes matter\n  independently.\n- Do not exclude evidence solely because it concerns a related period, population or product variant. Assess whether it can inform\n  the open question, preserving the difference in the record. Do not present a forecast for a later year as a forecast for the\n  thesis's year. If another open thesis covers the evidence more directly, consider that thesis as well; do not assume different\n  periods are automatically the same thesis or automatically unrelated.\n\nExamples of linking evidence to research:\n\n- Supply chain: an open thesis asks whether a manufacturer's production is constrained. A named supplier announces a capacity\n  expansion for a component the manufacturer uses. Link the announcement as a potential supply signal; it does not establish\n  allocations or deliveries.\n- Geopolitics: an open thesis asks whether an exporter can sell in a specified market. The relevant government proposes a licensing\n  restriction on that product. Link the proposal as evidence about market access; a proposal is not an enacted restriction.\n- Macro: an open thesis asks whether a company's borrowing costs will rise. The item reports that its floating-rate debt is tied to a\n  benchmark that has risen. Link the benchmark movement and the stated exposure; do not calculate the expense change unless the\n  source supports it.\n- Competition: an open thesis asks whether a company can retain customers in a product market. A named competitor cuts the price of a\n  competing product. Link the price cut as competitive evidence; do not assert lost customers or share without support.\n\n3. WHEN TO PROPOSE A NEW THESIS\n\nA thesis is a question a senior analyst would hold a card for: its answer could change a position because it could change the\ncompany's revenue, profit, cash or credit risk, or competitive position in a way you can name; public material will settle it on a\ndate; and no open thesis already asks it. A thesis asks one quantity for one period, or one event. It opens for one of five reasons, a closed set; a matter that fits none of them is\nevidence, kept and linked to the theses it informs or left unlinked, never a thesis:\n- main_driver: the company's own annual revenue or gross margin, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company\n  guides it: the revenue that carries the business, in total or of its main segment, or the gross margin (\"the bank's net interest\n  income this fiscal year\"; \"the retailer's same-store sales next fiscal year\"). It is not every line of the statements. Name the\n  measure, its scope and the fiscal year; a level and its growth rate are one thesis when the same reported figure settles both.\n  The material that publishes the figure, usually the annual report, settles it.\n- product_node: when the generation of the main product that carries the company's value reaches the step that brings revenue,\n  usually first shipments; announcements and samples are its evidence, and only milestones an analyst bets on separately (a drug's\n  trial result and its approval) are separate theses (\"will the carmaker's new platform start deliveries in 2026?\";\n  \"will the drugmaker's next-generation inhaler, the product line that carries its value, reach pharmacies by mid-2027?\").\n- binding_obligation: an obligation the company takes on in its own name, large enough to change its revenue, profit, cash or credit\n  risk: guaranteeing, backing or giving credit support for another party's debt, lease, revenue or capacity, lending to it,\n  committing to buy capacity or services, or a sized stake or acquisition not yet completed. One already undertaken is tracked by its\n  amount at the next annual report; one not yet signed by whether it is signed by a check date within 18 months of the item (\"how much will the\n  utility have guaranteed for its project companies' loans at its next annual report?\"; \"will the retailer sign a guarantee for its\n  franchisees' leases, large enough to change its credit risk, by the check date?\"). Its own borrowing or leases and a completed\n  or unsized investment are not obligations.\n- shared_quantity: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies depend on, for this or next calendar year:\n  several companies' combined output or spending, a contract price, an interest rate (\"the largest container lines' combined capacity\n  added in 2026\"; \"next year's average contract price of a raw material\"). Another population or wording of the same aggregate is\n  evidence for it.\n- policy_stage: the step a policy or regulatory process reaches, naming who decides (\"will the regulator approve the drug for a second\n  indication?\"; \"will the government require licences for the product's exports by a date?\").\n\n- Open only matters an analyst would bet on separately; small matters open no thesis and their statements are kept as evidence. A\n  customer's deployment plan is evidence for the company's demand and product theses, unless it changes the company's own cash or\n  credit risk, which is judged as an obligation.\n- Give the date the item supports. When it gives none, use the date the reason fixes and say how it was set: an obligation already\n  undertaken, its next annual report; an unsigned obligation, a check date within 18 months of the item; a pending regulatory\n  decision, the current fiscal year-end; a main_driver quantity, the release of that fiscal year's results. A shared quantity takes its release date and a product event the date its outcome can be\n  checked, only when the item supports one. A question no date can settle is rewritten or not opened.\n- Do not open a thesis about: an executive appointment or organisational change; the company's own borrowing or leases as an\n  obligation; a buyback authorisation or dividend declaration; a quarter's figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a\n  financial measure that is not a main_driver quantity, on its own; an undated moat or strategy; a feature, content or software update, price point, regional service or variant of a\n  product already on sale; another estimate, source or wording of what an open thesis tracks; an annual quantity after next year (an\n  obligation excepted); shareholder votes, bylaws or routine litigation procedure. Their statements are evidence for the theses they\n  inform, or left unlinked.\n- Before proposing a new thesis, name its reason (opens_as), the public material that will settle it (settled_by), and the closest\n  open thesis with why an analyst would bet on the two separately because their answers can move apart; with no open thesis, say so.\n  If the two cannot move apart, link the evidence to every open thesis it informs instead.\n\nCounterexamples:\n\n- \"The company's outlook is interesting\" or \"the industry may change\" is too vague: it names no outcome later evidence can inform.\n- If an open thesis tracks sales growth, a revised sales forecast is evidence for it; do not open a second thesis to repeat it.\n- A customer expanding capacity informs demand; it is not a thesis of its own, and not a claim that the supplier has received orders.\n- \"Is the stock attractively valued?\" is an investment conclusion, not a research question about the business.\n\n4. HOW TO WRITE EVIDENCE\n\n- One evidence item records one statement, and that statement is what you judge: a figure, date or comparison in the neighbouring\n  words does not make another claim in the same passage new or material. A statement told in several sentences of the item, with its\n  terms, figures and conditions, is one item.\n- Write a standalone summary: who did or said what, how much and for which period, naming the measure even when a neighbouring\n  sentence gives it. Preserve conditions, uncertainty and attribution. Return every passage the summary rests on, each copied\n  verbatim and contiguously from the item, without translation; do not join distant passages with an ellipsis.\n- Name the actor in the summary and identify the original party whose action, figure or claim it is. Give the reporting speaker when\n  available. The item's publisher and publication date come from its source metadata.\n- Use only this item's information. Distinguish forecasts, allegations and unconfirmed reports from confirmed outcomes. Report plans\n  as plans; do not infer committed funding, orders, deliveries or revenue.\n- For each item, return its evidence tier, the original statement date and the period the statement describes. These are separate\n  pieces of information.\n\nEVIDENCE TIER\n\nClassify the statement by what is confirmed, not how important it is:\n\n- rumour: the item attributes the claim to unnamed sources or calls it unconfirmed.\n- fact: an official action, published actual figure or completed transaction, including an announcement or completed transaction\n  reported by an article.\n- party_statement: a company's guidance, management statement or official's remarks. A forecast is a statement, not a completed\n  outcome.\n- third_party_view: an analyst's, journalist's or expert's opinion or estimate.\n\nApply the first matching category in that order. An unnamed-source or unconfirmed claim remains a rumour even if it describes an\naction or number. If none matches and the claim is unattributed, use rumour. The tier is not an importance score.\n\nEVIDENCE TIME\n\n- statement_date: the original statement's full day in YYYY-MM-DD when known; otherwise null. Do not use the article date as the\n  original date unless the statement was made in the originating party's own release, filing, call or analysis. Do not assign that\n  date to an older statement quoted there.\n- statement_date_text: the original date or partial date as stated, if present; otherwise null. Preserve a month or relative date\n  without inventing a day. A forecast horizon or an occasion is not a date.\n- evidence_period: the period the reported fact, plan or forecast covers, as supported by the item; otherwise null. This is not the\n  statement date.\n\nReturn the theses and evidence in the supplied response schema, after the closing check at the end of this request. Return empty\nlists when nothing passes.\nBefore you return the answer, check it once. Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy. Ask first whether it is new: repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise. Do not drop a reported step, figure, guidance, forecast or decision because the item retells it or another outlet reported it before: a later step compares each statement with the evidence already stored and records a repeat there. Guidance, a forecast, a plan or a decision still in force keeps its place even when retold, including a change to a plan, design or schedule that another outlet reported days or weeks before. Judge the action or information itself, not its verb tense, and do not take a statement as old because its date is missing. Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item. A missing amount, date or scale never drops an item on its own: a forecast, a rumour, a counter-example or a distant or conditional statement is judged like any other.\nThese are not kept, even when a named party states them. What a row says it does not cover goes back to the test above, unless the row says it is kept:\n- background the analyst already knew, such as the company's history (\"the company was founded in 1998\"); an arrangement the item only describes as in place, even when no date is given: customers or partners that use, host, run or have built on the company's products, and the benefits they describe from that use (\"two airlines fly the planemaker's jets\"; \"three insurers run claims on the company's software and report faster payouts\"); a partnership, contract, plant or investment the item itself dates to an earlier month or year with no new step (\"earlier this year the company partnered with the glassmaker on three plants\"; \"in May it signed a $3 billion cloud contract\"); it does not cover a step the item reports as news, taken, decided, planned or under way (an order, a selection, an integration, an expansion, a deployment), even when it gives no date (\"the retailer's largest supplier is opening its own stores, people familiar said this week\"; \"the two largest cement makers are adding kilns to meet demand\"), nor a customer's, supplier's or partner's newly disclosed revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amount; a deal the item mentions as already existing is an arrangement in place even with its amount (\"a rival airline already leases 40 of the same jets\");\n- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\n- a product, game, driver or benchmark specification with no business scale (\"the vacuum runs 60 minutes on a charge\"; \"a benchmark score\"), a retail price detail (\"a retailer marks one model down by $50\"), and a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes (\"the maker says its drug works twice as fast as older ones\"; \"a reviewer's test\"); it does not cover a competitor's comparison against the company's product, a partner's or customer's adoption or integration (also when a comparison shares its sentence), a reported launch, shipment, delay or cancellation of any of the company's products or a change to a product plan or configuration, including a reported sign that a planned product is going ahead (\"the long-range version of the jet is likely delayed or limited to a few deliveries\"; \"a parts supplier's catalogue lists the unannounced model\"), nor the company's decision to change the price it charges; uncertainty or a smaller product line does not make it a specification;\n- an unargued view or a quote that only characterises (\"the stock is a hold\"; \"a pivotal moment\"; \"an industry-leading platform\"), and a named analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation (\"the recall shows quality risks are rising\"); it does not cover a reading that adds a new fact or calculation, nor the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands (\"the carmaker said the launch date has not moved\"), which is judged as the plan itself would be; a target price or valuation of the company is not kept, even with its assumptions and derivation, while the estimates it rests on are judged on their own (an analysts' earnings forecast is kept);\n- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\n- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\n- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\nA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\nReturn only the evidence items you keep.\nThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\nFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the five reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\nAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n{\n \"type\": \"object\",\n \"additionalProperties\": false,\n \"required\": [\n  \"new_theses\",\n  \"evidence\"\n ],\n \"properties\": {\n  \"new_theses\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"description\",\n     \"outcome\",\n     \"period\",\n     \"opens_as\",\n     \"settled_by\",\n     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"description\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n     },\n     \"outcome\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n     },\n     \"period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n     },\n     \"opens_as\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"main_driver\",\n       \"product_node\",\n       \"binding_obligation\",\n       \"shared_quantity\",\n       \"policy_stage\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the five in section 3.\"\n     },\n     \"settled_by\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n     },\n     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n     },\n     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  },\n  \"evidence\": {\n   \"type\": \"array\",\n   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n   \"items\": {\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"required\": [\n     \"local_id\",\n     \"summary\",\n     \"source_passages\",\n     \"original_party\",\n     \"reporting_speaker\",\n     \"tier\",\n     \"statement_date\",\n     \"statement_date_text\",\n     \"evidence_period\",\n     \"links\",\n     \"figures\"\n    ],\n    \"properties\": {\n     \"local_id\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n     },\n     \"summary\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n     },\n     \"source_passages\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"string\"\n      }\n     },\n     \"original_party\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Party whose action, figure or claim is reported; null if unknown. Use the reporting outlet or author as the original party only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report.\"\n     },\n     \"reporting_speaker\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Person or outlet making or reporting the statement in this item, when known; null if unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\",\n        \"pattern\": \"^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original statement day as YYYY-MM-DD when known; null if the full day is unknown.\"\n     },\n     \"figures\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"measure\",\n        \"period\",\n        \"value\",\n        \"kind\",\n        \"basis\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"measure\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The financial measure as the passage states it.\"\n        },\n        \"period\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"The period as stated; null when none is given.\"\n        },\n        \"value\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"The figure copied exactly from one of this item's passages, with its unit.\"\n        },\n        \"kind\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"actual\",\n          \"guidance\",\n          \"estimate\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"actual: reported, including a balance as of a date; guidance: the company's own outlook; estimate: a named party's or consensus forecast.\"\n        },\n        \"basis\": {\n         \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n           \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n           \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Scope and qualifications as stated (GAAP or non-GAAP, segment or company, conditions); null when none.\"\n        }\n       }\n      },\n      \"description\": \"The company's own useful financial figures this statement states (section 2, CONDITION); empty for any other statement. A statement with several useful figures stays one item and lists them all.\"\n     },\n     \"links\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\",\n      \"minItems\": 0,\n      \"description\": \"The existing or proposed theses this evidence informs; empty when it is material but no thesis takes it yet: it is kept in the company's record and linked when a covering thesis opens.\",\n      \"items\": {\n       \"type\": \"object\",\n       \"additionalProperties\": false,\n       \"required\": [\n        \"target_type\",\n        \"target_id\",\n        \"relevance\"\n       ],\n       \"properties\": {\n        \"target_type\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"enum\": [\n          \"existing\",\n          \"new\"\n         ],\n         \"description\": \"Whether the reference identifies an open thesis or a new proposal.\"\n        },\n        \"target_id\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"Exact supplied ID when existing, or local_id of a new thesis in this answer.\"\n        },\n        \"relevance\": {\n         \"type\": \"string\",\n         \"description\": \"How this evidence informs the referenced thesis, distinguishing source claims from inference.\"\n        }\n       }\n      }\n     },\n     \"tier\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"enum\": [\n       \"fact\",\n       \"party_statement\",\n       \"third_party_view\",\n       \"rumour\"\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Source tier of the statement; an unconfirmed or unnamed-source claim takes precedence as rumour.\"\n     },\n     \"statement_date_text\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Original date or partial date as stated in the item; null when absent.\"\n     },\n     \"evidence_period\": {\n      \"anyOf\": [\n       {\n        \"type\": \"string\"\n       },\n       {\n        \"type\": \"null\"\n       }\n      ],\n      \"description\": \"Period the fact, plan or forecast describes, as supported by the item; null when unknown.\"\n     }\n    }\n   }\n  }\n }\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '250,420p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">问题（观点）</td><td>账本里追踪的一件事：一个问题句、一组结果档、一个到期日，写下后不改<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">候选问题</td><td>抽取这一步提议新开的问题</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">标的问题、主题问题</td><td>标的：答案是一家可交易公司（或币、商品）自己的经营结果。主题：答案是世界上的一件事，影响很多公司<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">结果档</td><td>一个问题事先固定、互不重叠、覆盖全部结果的结局，五档或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 rung</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">来源层</td><td>事实、当事人陈述、第三方观点、传闻<span class=\"src\">PRD 06；英文 evidence tier</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">分量</td><td>一条证据对判断有多重要：核心、辅助、可选、不收<span class=\"src\">第 6 节；D243</span>。Alex 说的\"档位低一点\"指它</td><td>结果档、来源层</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究用途</td><td>判断这一步引用一条证据去支持一个具体结论时，它撑得住多强：直接可用、有条件可用、线索、不可用<span class=\"src\">D221，第 7 节</span></td><td>分量</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">七类驱动</td><td>一条陈述为什么对公司业务重要的七条路径<span class=\"src\">D208</span>。需求：客户要买多少，如订单、客户支出、贷款需求、客流。供给与投入：能做出多少、成本多少，如产能、原料和零部件价格、燃料、矿石品位。竞争与份额：对手的产品、价格、开店、赢单。定价与装机：公司能收多少价、存量多大，如售价、费率、利差、装机量、存量客户。产品周期：发布、出货、试验、获批、延期。政策：法规、许可、关税、利率、监管决定。资本与义务：融资、担保、承诺、投资、收购</td><td>问题类型</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">市场预期与估值</td><td>市场已经定价了什么：估值倍数、市值、目标价、股价反应。观点的立场要和它比<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §8</span>。对一个业务量的一致预期（收入、EPS）是那个业务量的证据，不归这里</td><td>七类驱动</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究组</td><td>几个问题共同在追的一件正在进行的事<span class=\"src\">D165</span></td><td>问题</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本里记三种东西</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>证据</b>一条记录一个陈述，一件事用几句话说仍是一条<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；Alex 判 11</span>。记逐字引文、能单独读懂的一句话摘要、说话人、原始说话人和原始日期（不知道就写不知道，不填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>）、来源层。同一条证据可以挂到几个问题上，推力写在挂接上<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。每一条进来的证据都单独存下；和已有证据的关系（同一说法、修订）由匹配标出，作为意见，两条都留着<span class=\"src\">D202、D204</span>。原始说话人、原始日期、数字都相同的几条（说话人或日期不知道的不算相同），由代码认作同一条：判断时只给看一次，写明几家报道，每条仍照存<span class=\"src\">D248 第 7 条；改 D204 的\"两条都给判断看\"</span>。这条在打开之前要先在同一说法的金标上量两件事（金标按这条规则实际会合的组取，对着原文读）：它会不会藏掉不同或更丰富的说法（比如多一句限定），它依赖的原始说话人、原始日期两个字段准不准；量完之前，照 D204 两条都给判断看。</li>\n<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n\n<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n<li><b>口径完整：</b>算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚；支出、融资、担保、订单、收入不混。</li>\n<li><b>时间正确：</b>原文支持这个期间，不把几年的平均写成今年。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>不开</th><th>出处</th><th>它变成什么</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>季度数字和季度指引</td><td>第 1 版 §6；PRD 06 梯子第 6 条</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一段指引里的每一行（\"费用率、税率是模型输入，不是争论\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>没日期的\"护城河\"\"战略\"</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>高管任免、股东投票、回购授权；章程</td><td>第 1 版 §6；章程出自 D239 选定的 role-v29 原文（\"executive appointments, shareholder votes or bylaws\"）</td><td>证据或不留</td></tr>\n<tr><td>例行诉讼程序</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>客户的部署计划（\"它是供应商需求和产品问题的证据，除非改变供应商自己的现金或信用风险\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据；改变公司自己的现金或信用风险时按 C 类判</td></tr>\n<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>把远期年度预测改装成事件</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>后年及以后的年度量（约束性义务除外）</td><td>PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；D185</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一个量的另一个估计、另一种口径、另一个来源</td><td>第 1 版 §6 测试 4</td><td>那个已开问题的证据，由匹配并入</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n<li><b>同一个计划的几种说法</b>（担保、融资承诺、信用支持……），最后核对的是同一个数，是一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一代产品的几个里程碑：</b>一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>身份：</b>事件和政策题里模型写的期间起点，不拿来挡合并；对象、事件、截止日照旧核对<span class=\"src\">D248 第 5 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>续期：</b>同一个量或同一串事件的下一个期间<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Succession、D190</span>。</li>\n<li><b>另一题：</b>同一件事里答案能分开走、分析员会分别下注的：有自己驱动的组成部分；同一笔交易或同一份附注里两个各自会变、分别盯着的数；另一件事<span class=\"src\">D190 碰撞裁决的四种；D248 第 1 条收窄了\"担保和融资\"</span>。</li>\n<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\n<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>谁判，谁查</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>内容</th><th>谁</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\n<tr><td>结果档形状、期间是真日期、到期在文章之后、季度数、年限、约束性义务 18 个月、<code>settled_by</code> 不为空</td><td>代码：只查形状，不判重要性<span class=\"src\">D154、D155、D184</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"note\">年限按公司财年数：2026 年 7 月时 NVIDIA 在 FY2027（2027 年 1 月结束），所以 FY2028 是明年。代码原来按自然年算，把 FY2028 当成后年拒掉；在 v29 答案的 40 个带年份的候选里拒错了 2 个。已修，测试是 <span class=\"path\">tests/test_fiscal_year_horizon.py</span><span class=\"src\">D243</span>。</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"evidence\"><span class=\"num\">5</span>证据标准</h2>\n<h3>5.1 留的规则和四类</h3>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个在追这家公司的分析员，读到会在本周笔记里写下来，因为它让某个问题的答案更可能或更不可能。</b>问题不限于库里已有的，也不限于本公司：客户、供应商、竞争者、监管、宏观都算<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；D208 七类驱动</span>。</p></blockquote>\n<p><b>整体倾向谨慎，对增量敏感。</b>杂音很大，不是什么都要抽，不是什么都算线索。判一句话之前先问：这是新信息吗？它让哪个问题的答案变了？一件新发生的事、一个新数字、一个新的具体判断，是增量，不能漏；重复常识、描述长期状况、泛泛的看法，是杂音<span class=\"src\">D243</span>。增量和杂音的具体界线按 5.3 各行和边界一起判<span class=\"src\">D250</span>。</p>\n<p>从第一段读到最后一段，分析员会记的（按本节和 5.3 各行边界一起判）都留。一页有八条就是八条，不挑<span class=\"src\">D199</span>。它们通常是下面四类之一；四类描述的是会记的陈述长什么样，不是\"属于四类就一定留\"，留不留由上面的规则判；具体不留的行和边界见 5.3。</p>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>公司自己的数字、指引或决定</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"同店销售本季增长 4.2%\"；\"管理层把全年收入指引定在 120–130 亿美元\"；\"董事会批准 100 亿美元回购\"；\"公司取消软件订阅费，生产使用免费\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 8，Omniverse</span>。</li>\n<li><b>客户、供应商、竞争者、伙伴的有规模、有日期或有名字的动作，以及它们公布的数字</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2：三者有一个就够</span>第 1 版的例子\"Google Cloud 季度收入 248 亿美元，增长 82%，积压超过 5000 亿美元\"<span class=\"src\">Alex 判 11</span>；\"最大客户说明年订单砍五分之一\"；\"主要供应商说 2027 年产能翻倍\"；\"对手在欧洲降价 15%\"；\"一家银行选用竞争对手的系统\"；\"一家软件公司把本公司的模型集成进政府系统\"。后两条有名字、没金额，也留<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</li>\n<li><b>具名一方的主张或估计</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"CFO 说十年前建的工厂仍满负荷\"；\"分析师把明年 EPS 预期上调到 4.10 美元\"；\"做空机构指控公司虚增应收 20 亿美元\"；\"内存厂说 2027 年短缺最严重，持续到 2030\"。</li>\n<li><b>政策或监管的决定或步骤</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>\"监管机构批准该药第二个适应症\"；\"政府要求该产品出口须申请许可\"；\"25 家公司联名反对过早限制开放权重模型\"；\"财长说将调查某国公司是否窃取知识产权\"。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>典型的主张和背景</b><span class=\"src\">D243 第 5 条</span>：Alex 的原话是\"这种典型的主张背景属于常识，基本上抽出来也没有太多的意义除非带数字和具体的叙事不然都是属于不采纳\"。常识，就是跟这家公司的分析员读这篇之前就已经知道的：谁领先、谁在竞争、需求强、供给紧、融资难这类说法，和对已知状况的重述。这类陈述没有数字和具体的叙事就不收。不是常识的，是新信息，比如一份新报告的判断、一个新的市场数据、刚发生的事的细节，照上面的规则判，分析员会记就留。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>常识，不收：</b>\"博通 CEO 说能从英伟达抢份额\"；\"Blackwell 和 Rubin 仍然供不应求\"；\"融资会是扩大算力最大的障碍\"；\"内存厂避开了以往的产能过剩\"；\"博通预计明年随着新客户推出定制芯片大幅增长\"。</li>\n<li><b>新信息，收：</b>一位科技公司高管对媒体说\"中国国产 AI 芯片厂商已经全部卖光，客户在考虑性能更低的芯片\"；\"旧型号 GPU 的租金在涨\"；研究机构说\"这让 Rubin Ultra 暂时没有成熟的扩展方案，给对手留出了空间\"；\"华为现在占中国 AI 芯片市场约一半，这个市场约 500 亿美元\"。</li>\n<li><b>有数字也要过上面的规则：</b>作者说\"英特尔多年领先，占 CPU 市场 59%\"，和英伟达的问题关系不大，分析员不会记。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>5.2 不完整也是证据</h3>\n<p>预测、传闻、反证、远期、条件情景都是证据；它们的层级和确定性另记。不因为\"还没发生\"\"不是官方\"\"离现在远\"\"和我们方向相反\"就不留；一个真实的反例可能比十个顺风数字更重要<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2</span>。有名有姓的动作缺金额、缺日期也是证据，分量可以低一点<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。不留清单只按 5.3 各行和边界删，不能用来删掉标准要留的陈述：\"a reject rule never removes what the standard keeps\"<span class=\"src\">D240</span>。</p>\n\n<h3>5.3 不留的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2 的清单，加 D238、D243 的行</span></h3>\n<p>\"按同一行补的例子\"一列是我按同一行举的例子。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>不留</th><th>第 1 版的例子</th><th>按同一行补的例子</th><th>边界</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>没有业务规模的产品、游戏、驱动、跑分细节</td><td>\"这张卡 415W\"；\"Geekbench 跑分\"</td><td>接口、功率、旧型号的支持周期</td><td>对手拿它和本公司产品比的说法不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判（Alex 判 4：AMD 2.4 倍是辅助）；伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作不是产品细节（5.1 第 2 类）；公司自己、伙伴或第三方发布的对比（\"比闭源模型便宜 10 倍\"、\"同样功率多放 40% GPU\"、第三方测试）是产品细节，不收；同一句里伙伴、客户采用或集成的动作不因这一条删，照旧按 5.1 判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 3 条</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>股价涨跌、投资人仓位、技术面</td><td>\"本月跌 13%\"；\"Burry 做空\"</td><td>期权成交、基金买卖</td><td>股价反应背后的那条新闻不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判；\"财报后股价反应\"可选<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §10.2</span>；在研公司的估值倍数、市值、孤零零的目标价可选<span class=\"src\">D243 第 4 条</span>；别的股价涨跌照旧不留</td></tr>\n<tr><td>作者的一般性风险清单和没有推导的看法</td><td>\"如果 AI 退潮会受伤\"</td><td>\"这只股票该持有\"；\"芯片指数是纯粹的高估\"</td><td>有假设、有推导、有时点的条件估值要留<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §10.1</span>；具名分析师对一件已记下的事的解读（\"推迟会给对手留出窗口\"），没有新事实或推算的，不收，有新事实或推算的按 5.1 判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 4 条</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>记者的背景和框架</td><td>\"A100 2020 年上市\"；\"海湾国家花了几十亿但仍依赖它\"</td><td>\"公司成立于 1998 年\"；通用的技术讲解</td><td>没有数字和具体叙事的主张和背景不收；怎么分见 5.1<span class=\"src\">D243 第 5 条</span>；只描述一个现成安排（合作、客户在用、已有部署）、没有新动作的，是背景，不收，文中没写日期也一样<span class=\"src\">D250 第 1 条</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>没有数字也没有决定的政治、战略表态</td><td>\"分散供应商不能减少政治依赖\"</td><td>大使馆说\"立场一贯\"</td><td>官员宣布的政策步骤不能用这一行删掉，按 5.1 判（第 4 类）</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一事实的复述</td><td>一篇稿子用五句话说一个部署是一条；三家媒体转同一个独家，原始出处写同一个</td><td>标题和正文说同一件事</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>已知事实的重述</td><td>两个月后再说一遍 Q1 收入、指引、已公布的回购</td><td></td><td>抽取看不到库，只能从文字和日期看。重提的过去实际数可选；重提的季度指引和仍然有效的预测、计划按本来分量；看不出是旧事的不算重提<span class=\"src\">D243 第 6 条</span>；只描述现成安排、没有新动作的，按背景判（见\"记者的背景和框架\"一行），其余仍按这一行判<span class=\"src\">D250 第 1 条</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>模板</td><td>署名、作者简介、经纪商页脚、前瞻性声明、广告</td><td>页面上和本文无关的内容（相关文章预告、推荐列表、别的新闻标题）</td><td></td></tr>\n<tr><td>只有形容的引语</td><td></td><td>\"a pivotal moment\"；\"heterogeneous inference\"（role-v18 原文的例子）</td><td><span class=\"src\">D243 第 10 条</span></td></tr>\n<tr><td>新加坡转运案件的概况和被告个人资产</td><td></td><td></td><td>可选，收不收都不扣分<span class=\"src\">D231</span></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>另外一条来自后来的决定：<b>和公司所有市场都无关的别家公司的估值、股价、交易</b>不留（D238：\"another company's valuation, share price or deals that touch none of the company's markets\"）。别家公司的动作和经营数字不能用这一行删掉，它们留不留按 5.1 的规则判：要说得出它通过需求、供给、竞争、定价这类路径动了在研公司的哪个问题；只因同一篇文章、同一场活动或同一个生态挨着、说不出这条路径的，不收<span class=\"src\">D250 第 2 条</span>。</p>\n<p>不在清单上的句子，用 5.1 的规则逐句判（分析员会不会记）；金标里把这类判断标出来供复核。</p>\n\n<h3>5.4 一条记录必须保住的意思<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，原样</span></h3>\n<p>六格里只填这一条用得上的<span class=\"src\">D220</span>。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>格</th><th>要保住</th><th>丢了就错的例子</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>谁</td><td>原始判断者；是本人估计还是别人实测</td><td>AMD 自己的模拟说成独立实测</td></tr>\n<tr><td>什么</td><td>业务、指标或动作</td><td>\"收入增长 82%\"丢了\"收入\"</td></tr>\n<tr><td>多少</td><td>金额、比例、数量</td><td>四家 7450 亿写成五家</td></tr>\n<tr><td>哪个期间</td><td>预测或事实覆盖的期间；\"今年\"按公司财年或自然年写都算对<span class=\"src\">D233</span>，余下时间不改成全年</td><td>\"今年余下时间\"改成 FY2027 全年</td></tr>\n<tr><td>什么条件</td><td>推导的假设；计划、上限、\"最多\"</td><td>\"最多 4 万颗\"写成已部署 4 万颗</td></tr>\n<tr><td>预测还是已发生</td><td>指引、预计、商谈、传闻不等于已实现、已签约</td><td>\"商谈 6000 亿\"写成\"已承诺\"</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>原始发言日不知道就写不知道，不能填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>。一条记录单独读要能懂，条件不能只放在旁边另一条里<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3，引主分支 D251；两个分支的决定编号各自独立，D227</span>。不必要的：转述机构、普通发言场合、付费方案全名；漏了不扣原意分，<b>编造了仍算记录错误</b><span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §3</span>。没有来源证实的结论，可以作为分析员的推断写出，但不能写成来源说的事实<span class=\"src\">D218</span>。</p>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '4107,4127p;5571,5584p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '主驱动量|问题怎么写|同一题|开题测试|开题|</section>' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '4107,4127p;5571,5584p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n '主驱动量|问题怎么写|同一题|开题测试|开题|</section>' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html\"","aggregated_output":"## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n\n- Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\". On the\n  recommendation to keep a useful company figure no view takes as a condition of the company, he replied \"好\". Record:\n  `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §§16–17.\n\n## D383 · 2026-11-08 · D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later\n\n- Alex chose \"先存着，有观点再挂\": a statement the model judges useful but no thesis takes yet is kept in the company's record, linked when\n  a related thesis opens; what the closing check rejects is still dropped, including the cash flow he ruled out. Amends D209 beyond D382.\n  Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §27.\n\n## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\n\n- Alex chose \"按金标：只开大事\": a thesis opens only for the standard's reasons (an obligation the company takes on, its main product's\n  next node, a policy step, a checkable shared quantity); another company's single project, partnership or product line is evidence.\n  The reader-based small/fragment line gives way to must_open covered and must_not not opened. Class A (main-driver quantity) stays\n  out under D382. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §36.\n\n## D385 · 2026-11-08 · Target prices and valuation conclusions are not kept\n\n## D490 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a test: the new system may open questions on the company's revenue and margin\n\n- **Asked** (after D489, his reply to this exact question): \"这一周的对比显示：现行系统会为营收、毛利率开问题；新系统按你之前定的规则（D382：财务数字是条件，不是\n  问题）不开，所以两组盲评读者都列出的 5 件大事里它少了 3 件（FY2027 营收、FY2028 营收、FY2028 毛利率），145 条公司财务数字没有被任何判断读到。新系统接下来怎么处理营收\n  和毛利率？\" Options: test opening such questions (recommended); keep the rule; open none but use the figures.\n- **Alex:** \"试开这类问题 (Recommended)\". The option as shown to him: \"先在这周已存的文章上花几美分试：能否开出这 3 个问题，同时不乱开、不重复；通过后再跑第二个没用过的\n  新鲜周。会改变你的 D382/D384。历史上类似的放开曾多开 7 个不该开的问题（那次同时改了三处）。\"\n- **Decided:** a test arm of clean Step 1 is opened (a new version of the frozen c8 request, for this test only; c8 stays the adopted\n  request until a result is adopted). D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path; the arm departs from them on one point, the\n  company's main numbers as questions. First a probe of a few cents on the stored week's states, with its lines and stop condition written\n  before any send and a council round before the send (AGENTS §7.3); the second fresh week runs only if the probe meets its lines.\n\n3:<title>Hivemind 抽取与开题标准</title>\n130:    <li><a href=\"#opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</a></li>\n145:  <h1>抽取与开题标准</h1>\n155:  <dt>开题</dt>\n160:</section>\n194:<tr><td>2</td><td>\"共同量\"按 D191 落实：任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格（合计支出、合约价、利率）都可以开题，开题理由叫 <code>shared_quantity</code>；期间按自然年。提示词和代码要跟着改</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 D 类</td></tr>\n208:<p>Alex 逐个听了例子、逐个选的，七个都选 A；改了第 2、3、4 节，标准升为第 4 版，金标要按第 4 版重推：开题部分逐条重判，证据部分逐条核对（D244）。</p>\n213:<tr><td>1</td><td>同一个计划的几种说法，最后核对同一个数的，是一题；各自会变、会分别盯的数才分开；属于已按金额开题的计划的一笔交易并进去</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n216:<tr><td>4</td><td>公司自己的量只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 4 节</td></tr>\n218:<tr><td>6</td><td>单笔交易、产品、项目，规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开题；够不上的不开题，它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判，留下的是证据</td><td class=\"nowrap\">第 3 节 C 类、第 4 节</td></tr>\n233:<p>尺子跟着修：金标的证据部分按第 5 版重推、另存冻结，打分程序遇到证据部分版本对不上就拒绝打分；开题部分重推之前不报开题的分（第 8 节）。</p>\n253:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">开题理由</td><td>候选问题值得开的几类理由之一，答案里写在 <code>opens_as</code><span class=\"src\">D184；英文 admission reason</span></td><td></td></tr>\n266:<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n267:<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\n269:<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n272:<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n274:<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n276:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n278:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n296:<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n297:<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n300:<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n308:<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n310:<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n315:<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n318:<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n337:<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n343:<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n345:<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n346:<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n350:<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n354:<li><b>约束性义务：</b>\"一笔或一个计划\"一题<span class=\"src\">D210</span>；一笔交易是不是某个已按金额开题的计划的一部分，由匹配判，是就并入<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。还没签的单笔交易是\"签不签\"的是非题，照旧可以开，不并进计划的金额题<span class=\"src\">D210；PRD 06；D248 未改</span>。</li>\n355:<li><b>共同量：</b>以共同量理由开题、带量的候选（量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算），由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判同一题；政策阶段和别的事件保留按事件判的身份；不带这个开题理由的主题量由模型判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>。</li>\n362:<tr><td>测试 1–3、同一篇文章里的测试 4、属于哪一类、问题怎么写</td><td>抽取的模型（判断）</td></tr>\n364:<tr><td>和库里的同一题、续期、另一题</td><td>匹配（Jev）和碰撞裁决<span class=\"src\">D190</span>；共同量由代码<span class=\"src\">D197</span></td></tr>\n472:<p class=\"note\">下面这份第 3 版金标是历史记录。第 4 版（D248）改了开题的规则，没有改动证据条目（逐条核对见 <span class=\"path\">research/2026-10-30-noise/gold-v4-evidence-check.md</span>）；第 5 版（D250）改了证据的四条界线。金标的证据部分按第 5 版重推，两位互不知情的读者逐条判，分歧对着原文定，另存成新文件冻结，每条改动写改前、改后和理由，第 3 版文件不动（D243 第 11 条）。开题部分要按第 4 版逐条重判，重判之前打分程序不报开题的分；证据部分版本对不上，打分程序拒绝打分（D244、D250）。</p>\n487:<li><b>问题：</b>必须开的（类、开题理由、标的或主题、要点、<code>settled_by</code>）；可以开的（另一种合理写法）；不该开的（第 4 节哪一行或哪个测试）。</li>\n531:<li><b>每一句都对得上这一页。</b>提示词里每一句关于留、不留、分量、开题的话，在这一页找得到出处；找不到的，是给 Alex 的提议，不是改动<span class=\"src\">AGENTS §6</span>。</li>\n605:<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">10-29 D241</td><td class=\"nowrap\">这份标准</td><td>\"几个大类型的账本 - 开题标准和档次 这两个要完整的定义好写好\"；\"档位根据信息量作定标 -以上有你自己trace 过的golden set 来做为改prompt测试标准\"</td></tr>\n617:<tr><td>B2</td><td>主驱动量含不含产品节点</td><td>含，写成 A、B 两类</td><td>D236（在 D184 之后）</td></tr>\n618:<tr><td>B3</td><td>约束性义务：一笔或一个计划一题（D210），还是一组入股是一个判断（D201 规则 G）</td><td>按 D210 \"一笔或一个计划\"；一笔交易属不属于已开的计划，由匹配判；同一计划的几种说法是一题；够不上公司规模的单笔交易不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判</td><td>D210、D236、D238、D248</td></tr>\n619:<tr><td>B4</td><td>开题测试三套，提示词和代码都没用</td><td>第 1 版 §6 四个测试加评审三条写法检查（第 4 节）；测试 4 和库比的部分归匹配</td><td>第 1 版 §6；评审 §1；D211</td></tr>\n627:<tr><td>B12</td><td>研究组、驱动层</td><td>研究组不是问题，不代替开题判断；七类驱动是重要性的理由；词汇表只禁 \"thesis driver\"</td><td>D165、D208；评审 §6</td></tr>\n629:<tr><td>B14</td><td>组成部分算不算同一题</td><td>同一总量的另一种人群或口径是同一题；有自己驱动、答案能分开走、分析员会分别下注的是另一题，要过独立意义测试</td><td>D190；第 1 版 §6；D248</td></tr>\n652:<p>新案例上留不留的一致率从第二轮的 80–94% 升到 93–98%，连分量从 72–87% 升到 81–89%。剩下的分歧几乎都在核心和辅助的界线，由 D243 第 1 条定下判法。三位读者判对、作者判错的，记作作者的错：最大客户带来的收入和中国销售占比不该开题（独立意义测试），还有两处陈述。记录在 <span class=\"path\">simulation-log.md</span>。</p>\n655:<p>Codex 只读，逐条对照签过的第 1 版、全部决策、PRD 06，找\"作者自己加的规则\"、和决策矛盾的地方、引错的原话。每一轮的发现都改掉并记下处理。第一轮查出 18 处自己加的规则和 9 处和决策矛盾，比如\"名单外公司的量不开题\"违反 D155、D187，\"抽取要和库里比重复\"违反 D211，把达标线缩短，把\"在谈的金额\"排除出核心。最后三轮只剩措辞层面的问题；第十一轮的发现在 2.14 版改掉，没有再复查。</p>\n687:<footer>Hivemind · 抽取与开题标准 · 第 5 版 · 2026-10-29 Alex 签字（D243），2026-10-30 按 Alex 逐个选的七条修订（D248），2026-10-31 按 Alex 定的证据四条界线和计数单位修订（D250）。页首的 standard-version 是规则的版本号：改任何一条规则都要升它，金标随之重定，打分程序遇到版本对不上就拒绝打分（D244）。</footer>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The revised text addresses several issues from the first audit, but the date instruction still needs closer scrutiny: naming the results release does not necessarily give the model a supported calendar date. I’m checking that against the output fields and the standard’s limits on setting dates."}}
