{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json | sed -n '1,140p'; nl -ba clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-closing.txt\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t{\n     2\t \"type\": \"object\",\n     3\t \"additionalProperties\": false,\n     4\t \"required\": [\n     5\t  \"new_theses\",\n     6\t  \"evidence\"\n     7\t ],\n     8\t \"properties\": {\n     9\t  \"new_theses\": {\n    10\t   \"type\": \"array\",\n    11\t   \"description\": \"New thesis proposals, each referenced by at least one evidence link.\",\n    12\t   \"items\": {\n    13\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n    14\t    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    15\t    \"required\": [\n    16\t     \"local_id\",\n    17\t     \"description\",\n    18\t     \"outcome\",\n    19\t     \"period\",\n    20\t     \"opens_as\",\n    21\t     \"settled_by\",\n    22\t     \"closest_open_thesis\",\n    23\t     \"why_a_separate_bet\"\n    24\t    ],\n    25\t    \"properties\": {\n    26\t     \"local_id\": {\n    27\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    28\t      \"description\": \"Local reference for this new thesis in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n    29\t     },\n    30\t     \"description\": {\n    31\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    32\t      \"description\": \"The proposed research question, stated clearly.\"\n    33\t     },\n    34\t     \"outcome\": {\n    35\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    36\t      \"description\": \"The outcome or event being tracked by this thesis.\"\n    37\t     },\n    38\t     \"period\": {\n    39\t      \"anyOf\": [\n    40\t       {\n    41\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n    42\t       },\n    43\t       {\n    44\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n    45\t       }\n    46\t      ],\n    47\t      \"description\": \"The period or check date that settles the thesis: the one the item supports, or the one its reason fixes (section 3), with how it was set.\"\n    48\t     },\n    49\t     \"opens_as\": {\n    50\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    51\t      \"enum\": [\n    52\t       \"main_driver\",\n    53\t       \"product_node\",\n    54\t       \"binding_obligation\",\n    55\t       \"shared_quantity\",\n    56\t       \"policy_stage\"\n    57\t      ],\n    58\t      \"description\": \"The reason this thesis opens, one of the five in section 3.\"\n    59\t     },\n    60\t     \"settled_by\": {\n    61\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    62\t      \"description\": \"The public material that will settle the answer on a date (a filing, an official decision, a shipment confirmation, a statistics release).\",\n    63\t      \"pattern\": \"\\\\S\"\n    64\t     },\n    65\t     \"closest_open_thesis\": {\n    66\t      \"anyOf\": [\n    67\t       {\n    68\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n    69\t       },\n    70\t       {\n    71\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n    72\t       }\n    73\t      ],\n    74\t      \"description\": \"Exact ID of the open thesis closest to this one; null when the open list is empty.\"\n    75\t     },\n    76\t     \"why_a_separate_bet\": {\n    77\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n    78\t      \"description\": \"Why an analyst would bet on this question separately from the closest open thesis: how their answers can move apart.\"\n    79\t     }\n    80\t    }\n    81\t   }\n    82\t  },\n    83\t  \"evidence\": {\n    84\t   \"type\": \"array\",\n    85\t   \"description\": \"Evidence statements extracted from this item, with their thesis links.\",\n    86\t   \"items\": {\n    87\t    \"type\": \"object\",\n    88\t    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    89\t    \"required\": [\n    90\t     \"local_id\",\n    91\t     \"summary\",\n    92\t     \"source_passages\",\n    93\t     \"original_party\",\n    94\t     \"reporting_speaker\",\n    95\t     \"tier\",\n    96\t     \"statement_date\",\n    97\t     \"statement_date_text\",\n    98\t     \"evidence_period\",\n    99\t     \"links\",\n   100\t     \"figures\"\n   101\t    ],\n   102\t    \"properties\": {\n   103\t     \"local_id\": {\n   104\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n   105\t      \"description\": \"Local reference for this evidence in the answer; not a database ID.\"\n   106\t     },\n   107\t     \"summary\": {\n   108\t      \"type\": \"string\",\n   109\t      \"description\": \"Standalone faithful summary naming the actor and preserving relevant figures, periods and conditions.\"\n   110\t     },\n   111\t     \"source_passages\": {\n   112\t      \"type\": \"array\",\n   113\t      \"minItems\": 1,\n   114\t      \"description\": \"Contiguous verbatim passages from this source item that jointly support the summary; return each passage separately.\",\n   115\t      \"items\": {\n   116\t       \"type\": \"string\"\n   117\t      }\n   118\t     },\n   119\t     \"original_party\": {\n   120\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   121\t       {\n   122\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n   123\t       },\n   124\t       {\n   125\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   126\t       }\n   127\t      ],\n   128\t      \"description\": \"Party whose action, figure or claim is reported; null if unknown. Use the reporting outlet or author as the original party only for its own estimate, analysis or unnamed-source report.\"\n   129\t     },\n   130\t     \"reporting_speaker\": {\n   131\t      \"anyOf\": [\n   132\t       {\n   133\t        \"type\": \"string\"\n   134\t       },\n   135\t       {\n   136\t        \"type\": \"null\"\n   137\t       }\n   138\t      ],\n   139\t      \"description\": \"Person or outlet making or reporting the statement in this item, when known; null if unknown.\"\n   140\t     },\n     1\tBefore you return the answer, check it once. Read each evidence item back as the analyst following the company and keep it when you would write it in this week's notes because it makes some question's answer more or less likely, about the company or its customers, suppliers, competitors, regulators or the economy. Ask first whether it is new: repeated common knowledge, a long-standing situation retold and an unargued view are noise. Do not drop a reported step, figure, guidance, forecast or decision because the item retells it or another outlet reported it before: a later step compares each statement with the evidence already stored and records a repeat there. Guidance, a forecast, a plan or a decision still in force keeps its place even when retold, including a change to a plan, design or schedule that another outlet reported days or weeks before. Judge the action or information itself, not its verb tense, and do not take a statement as old because its date is missing. Fitting one of the four kinds does not keep an item. A missing amount, date or scale never drops an item on its own: a forecast, a rumour, a counter-example or a distant or conditional statement is judged like any other.\n     2\tThese are not kept, even when a named party states them. What a row says it does not cover goes back to the test above, unless the row says it is kept:\n     3\t- background the analyst already knew, such as the company's history (\"the company was founded in 1998\"); an arrangement the item only describes as in place, even when no date is given: customers or partners that use, host, run or have built on the company's products, and the benefits they describe from that use (\"two airlines fly the planemaker's jets\"; \"three insurers run claims on the company's software and report faster payouts\"); a partnership, contract, plant or investment the item itself dates to an earlier month or year with no new step (\"earlier this year the company partnered with the glassmaker on three plants\"; \"in May it signed a $3 billion cloud contract\"); it does not cover a step the item reports as news, taken, decided, planned or under way (an order, a selection, an integration, an expansion, a deployment), even when it gives no date (\"the retailer's largest supplier is opening its own stores, people familiar said this week\"; \"the two largest cement makers are adding kilns to meet demand\"), nor a customer's, supplier's or partner's newly disclosed revenue, capacity, orders or contracted amount; a deal the item mentions as already existing is an arrangement in place even with its amount (\"a rival airline already leases 40 of the same jets\");\n     4\t- a typical claim that is common knowledge, without a figure and a specific account: that a firm leads or competes, that demand is strong or supply tight, a general risk (\"if demand slows it would hurt\"); a number does not lift a familiar position (\"the rival grocer has led this market for years and still holds 40%\"); it does not cover a dated forecast of a shortage, a price or demand (\"the steelmaker expects the shortage to peak next year and last until 2028\"), a competitor's newly reported share, volume or price in the company's market (\"the local rival now holds about half of the regional market, worth about $5 billion\"), nor a reported movement of a named price, rental rate, lead time or order book, even without a figure (\"rental rates for used trucks have been climbing this quarter\"); a general statement that demand stays strong or a product stays popular is not one;\n     5\t- a product, game, driver or benchmark specification with no business scale (\"the vacuum runs 60 minutes on a charge\"; \"a benchmark score\"), a retail price detail (\"a retailer marks one model down by $50\"), and a comparison the company, a partner or a third party publishes (\"the maker says its drug works twice as fast as older ones\"; \"a reviewer's test\"); it does not cover a competitor's comparison against the company's product, a partner's or customer's adoption or integration (also when a comparison shares its sentence), a reported launch, shipment, delay or cancellation of any of the company's products or a change to a product plan or configuration, including a reported sign that a planned product is going ahead (\"the long-range version of the jet is likely delayed or limited to a few deliveries\"; \"a parts supplier's catalogue lists the unannounced model\"), nor the company's decision to change the price it charges; uncertainty or a smaller product line does not make it a specification;\n     6\t- an unargued view or a quote that only characterises (\"the stock is a hold\"; \"a pivotal moment\"; \"an industry-leading platform\"), and a named analyst's reading of an event already recorded that adds no new fact or calculation (\"the recall shows quality risks are rising\"); it does not cover a reading that adds a new fact or calculation, nor the company's own statement that its plan, schedule or guidance still stands (\"the carmaker said the launch date has not moved\"), which is judged as the plan itself would be; a target price or valuation of the company is not kept, even with its assumptions and derivation, while the estimates it rests on are judged on their own (an analysts' earnings forecast is kept);\n     7\t- a political or strategic stance with no figure and no decision (\"diversifying suppliers will not reduce dependence\"); it does not cover a policy or regulatory step, nor a decision still in force that the item reports;\n     8\t- a share-price move, an investor's position or trade, or the market value (\"shares fell 13% this month\"; \"he is short the stock\"); it does not cover the news behind the move;\n     9\t- another company's matter that touches none of the company's markets (its valuation, share price, governance or a deal outside them), or that sits next to the company only by sharing an article, an event or an ecosystem; you supply the connection as the analyst and the item need not state it: a customer's spending, orders or backlog bears on demand, a supplier's capacity, output, prices or revenue on supply and input costs, a rival's products, prices or share in the company's markets on competition (\"a large customer's order backlog doubled\"; \"the main supplier's quarterly revenue jumped on demand for the part\");\n    10\t- the same fact said again in other words within this item: one deal, hire, programme or reported measure told in several sentences, with its terms, figures and growth rates, is one evidence item; keep the fuller wording (\"a $2 billion order for 120 stores in 15 countries over three years\"; \"cloud revenue of $8 billion, up 30% on the year and 6% on the quarter, 40% of the total\"); a deal one party signs under a wider programme, with its own amount or capacity, is its own evidence item, and a fact another outlet reported before is not a repeat within this item;\n    11\t- company boilerplate, bylines, forward-looking-statement text.\n    12\tA report and another party's denial or confirmation of it are two items, each kept only if it passes the test above; an estimate stays apart from any valuation drawn from it, and the valuation is not kept; one party's statement keeps its own planned or rumoured details.\n    13\tReturn only the evidence items you keep.\n    14\tThen check the theses and links. A new thesis that asks the same underlying question, about the same subject and scope, as an open thesis or another new thesis is not proposed: link its evidence to that thesis. A new thesis needs at least one kept evidence item, and a vague or noisy topic with no outcome to watch is not proposed. Each kept evidence item links to every thesis it informs and to no thesis its own relevance says it does not inform.\n    15\tFor each new thesis, check its opens_as, settled_by, closest_open_thesis and why_a_separate_bet: drop the thesis if it fits none of the five reasons in section 3, if no public material will settle it on a date, if an open thesis exists and its answer cannot move apart from it, or if it falls under a 'do not open' item in section 3; then link its evidence to every open thesis it informs, or leave it without links.\n    16\tAn item whose only home would be a new thesis that is not a big matter is returned with empty links and kept without links; an item an open thesis covers is linked there, not left without links. Then read back each statement you return with empty links that states the company's own figures: return it only if a figure can change what an analyst expects of the company's revenue, profitability, funding or credit risk, or competitive position; for example, a cash-rich company's balance or cash flow that the item ties to nothing usually cannot; return only what passes.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '260,350p' docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html; sed -n '4107,4126p;5571,5582p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"<tr><td class=\"nowrap\">研究组</td><td>几个问题共同在追的一件正在进行的事<span class=\"src\">D165</span></td><td>问题</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h2 id=\"ledger\"><span class=\"num\">2</span>账本里记三种东西</h2>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>证据</b>一条记录一个陈述，一件事用几句话说仍是一条<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §2；Alex 判 11</span>。记逐字引文、能单独读懂的一句话摘要、说话人、原始说话人和原始日期（不知道就写不知道，不填报道日<span class=\"src\">D220</span>）、来源层。同一条证据可以挂到几个问题上，推力写在挂接上<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。每一条进来的证据都单独存下；和已有证据的关系（同一说法、修订）由匹配标出，作为意见，两条都留着<span class=\"src\">D202、D204</span>。原始说话人、原始日期、数字都相同的几条（说话人或日期不知道的不算相同），由代码认作同一条：判断时只给看一次，写明几家报道，每条仍照存<span class=\"src\">D248 第 7 条；改 D204 的\"两条都给判断看\"</span>。这条在打开之前要先在同一说法的金标上量两件事（金标按这条规则实际会合的组取，对着原文读）：它会不会藏掉不同或更丰富的说法（比如多一句限定），它依赖的原始说话人、原始日期两个字段准不准；量完之前，照 D204 两条都给判断看。</li>\n<li><b>问题</b>问题句、结果档、到期日写下不改；当前判断随证据更新，到期定格<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。问题分标的和主题，按开题理由分五类（第 3 节）。问题从三处来：文章里的候选问题；用户的备忘录<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 State</span>：\"A thesis from the user's memo is not yet judged until evidence first links to it\"；分析员开始覆盖一家公司时种下的驱动问题<span class=\"src\">D208，设计未建</span>。</li>\n<li><b>研究组</b>一件正在进行的事（一个产品换代及其部署、一笔融资或收购、一个政策过程、一轮投资或需求周期），把几个问题组织在一起，常常跨公司。它不是问题，也不代替开题判断。公司自己的报表行（收入、毛利率、费用、税率、资本开支）不带研究组，除非这一行本身就在追这样一件事；它也可以加入别的问题建的组<span class=\"src\">D165</span>。</li>\n</ol>\n<p><b>不进账本的：</b>归档找不到家的证据，记 <code>no home</code> 扔掉<span class=\"src\">D209</span>。评估时逐条读被扔的，分四种：抽取的垃圾；库里缺这个问题（覆盖缺口）；问题在却没挂上（归档错）；该开没开（开题错）。各归各的环节<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §7</span>。存储的表结构归 PRD 06 管。</p>\n\n<h2 id=\"types\"><span class=\"num\">3</span>问题的五类：账本的几大类型</h2>\n<p>开题理由是 D184 定的四类，D236 把主驱动量扩到产品节点，所以写成五类。判两件事，互不顶替：这是谁的问题（标的还是主题）；为什么值得开（开题理由）。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap wide\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>类</th><th>开题理由</th><th>标的或主题</th><th>问什么</th><th>量还是事件</th><th>期间和到期</th><th>核对材料 <code>settled_by</code></th><th>出处</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>A</b> 主驱动量</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引：撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率、资本开支；跨行业如银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售、公用事业的费率基数、航空公司的燃油成本（当它是争论焦点时）。不是每一行报表数</td><td>量，五档</td><td>公司财年的今年或明年；到期日是这个数的发布日</td><td>公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报</td><td>D184：<code>settled_by</code> 是 \"the public material that resolves it\"；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>B</b> 主产品节点</td><td><code>main_driver</code></td><td>标的</td><td>承载公司价值的那一代产品哪天走到能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；发布、送样是它的证据，只有会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span></td><td>事件，五档，或是非两档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 1 条</span></td><td>能判出结果的那天</td><td>公司公告、发货确认</td><td>D236</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>C</b> 约束性义务</td><td><code>binding_obligation</code></td><td>标的</td><td>公司以自己名义承担的：为别人的债务、租约或收入担保或提供信用支持；借钱给别人；承诺购买（向别人买产能或服务也算）；为客户的产能或收入兜底；或写明规模、尚未完成的入股或收购<span class=\"src\">D236；收购按 D243 第 7 条</span>。规模要大到能改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险才开；够不上的单笔入股、收购、租约、授信不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条</span>。不算：自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。D239 选定的 role-v29 原文：\"Its own borrowing, its own leases and a completed or unsized investment are not obligations\"；D238 的记录写作 \"the company's own borrowing and leases and a completed or unsized stake do not\"</td><td>还没签：是非两档。已经承担（一笔或一个计划）：金额，五档</td><td>检查日最多在文章后 18 个月<span class=\"src\">D185</span>；已承担的按下一份年报</td><td>签约公告、年报承诺附注</td><td>D184、D185、D210、D236、D238、D243</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>D</b> 共同量</td><td><code>shared_quantity</code><span class=\"src\">D191、D243 第 2 条</span>；现行提示词和代码还叫 <code>industry_aggregate</code>，按这一页改</td><td>主题</td><td>任何一家公司之外、好几家都会受它影响的量或价格：几家公司的合计（云厂商资本开支）、价格（内存合约价、油价）、利率。同一总量的另一种人群、另一种说法是这个量的证据</td><td>量，五档</td><td>自然年的今年或明年。同一个量、同一年只有一个问题，由代码按\"主题＋量＋期间\"判<span class=\"src\">D197</span>；量的类别是 <code>other</code> 的不算</td><td>几家公司年报、统计发布、官方决定</td><td>D184、D191、D197、D243；PRD 06</td></tr>\n<tr><td class=\"nowrap\"><b>E</b> 政策阶段</td><td><code>policy_stage</code></td><td>问的是一家公司的收入、利润、份额或产品进度，算标的，即使由政策驱动；问的是世界上的事（许可制度、利率、合计支出），算主题。D184 采纳的 role-v12 原文：\"A question about a company's revenue, profit, share or product progress is an asset thesis; put its ticker in object, even when policy or macroeconomics drives it\"</td><td>一个政策或监管过程到了哪一步，写明谁说了算</td><td>事件，五档或两档</td><td>能判出那一步的那天。文章没写日期的待决监管事项，用本财年末（role-v12 原文：\"A pending regulatory decision may lack a date; use the current fiscal year-end as its due date\"）；这个日期是研究员定的检查日，要标明<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1 条</span></td><td>官方决定、公报</td><td>D184</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<p>例子（跨行业）：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>A：</b>NVIDIA FY2027 数据中心收入；一家地区银行 FY2026 净利息收入；一家公用事业公司 2027 年费率基数。</li>\n<li><b>B：</b>下一代机架系统能否在 2027 年底前开始出货；一家车企的新平台能否在 2026 年内开始交付。</li>\n<li><b>C：</b>NVIDIA 为云客户产能兜底的义务在 FY2027 年报达到多少；一家保险公司是否在 2027 年中前为合资公司 5 亿美元债务签署担保。</li>\n<li><b>D：</b>五家最大云厂商 2026 年合计资本开支；2027 年 DRAM 合约价相对 2026 年的变化、美联储 2026 年最后一次会议后的利率上限。</li>\n<li><b>E：</b>中国是否在 2027-01-31 前正式批准本国公司进口 H200；美国是否在某日前对某类芯片实行出口许可。这两题问的是许可这件世界上的事，所以是主题，role-v12 原文的例子就是 \"licensing\"。一个监管决定对一家公司收入或产品进度的影响，问成那家公司的量或产品节点时，是标的问题（同一句原文）。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>五类之外的东西去哪</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>七类驱动不是问题类型。</b>它们是一条陈述为什么重要的理由，用来判分量和归档。D208 设计的\"每家公司种下的驱动问题\"由分析员开始覆盖时写好，不从文章里开；还没建。</li>\n<li><b>别家公司自己的量</b>（对手的份额、客户的资本开支）：D187 定了\"任何公司自己的量是那家公司的问题，私营公司也算\"，但还没实现，要先在覆盖名单里加私营公司这一类。D155 定了\"公司清单可以作为初始参考，但清单外不能忽略\"。现行代码在匹配时跳过名单外的对象<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Step 4</span>。所以抽取照常可以提这样的问题，它要过第 4 节的测试；名单外的现在会被匹配跳过，这不算抽取错。</li>\n<li><b>宏观量</b>（利率、通胀）：按 D 类共同量开题<span class=\"src\">D243 第 2 条</span>。只来自一篇纯宏观文章时，只有主题在名单上才开<span class=\"src\">D191 第 3 条</span>。宏观对每家公司的正负，在判断那家公司时读主题块决定<span class=\"src\">D191 第 1 条、D195</span>。</li>\n<li><b>开题理由是封闭的</b><span class=\"src\">D184</span>：一件事属不属于五类之一，按上表逐条看，比如一个监管决定看它是不是 E 类。哪一类都不属于的不开；它是不是证据、挂到哪，照第 5 节和归档规则。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>问题怎么写：PRD 06 的梯子规则，不重写</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一个问题只问一个量的一个期间，或一件事；能各自朝相反方向走、而且分析员会分别下注的部分要分开<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 3 条；\"分别下注\"是 D248 加的，PRD 06 签字后更新</span>，分开的每一题都要过第 4 节的测试。</li>\n<li>写成问句，不写成断言<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 Rationale</span>。</li>\n<li>结果档可核对、不重叠、不留缝，到期恰好一档成立；中间一档写明和什么比；\"小幅\"\"部分\"这种不能核对的说法不用，部分状态写成单独一档<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 2 条</span>。标的问题的档描述业务结果；主题问题的档只写结局，不写好坏<span class=\"src\">PRD 06、D186</span>。</li>\n<li>到期日：量是它的发布日；事件是能判出结果的那天。公司的量用公司财年，别的用自然年，只开今年和明年<span class=\"src\">PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；约束性义务例外，D185</span>。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2 id=\"opening\"><span class=\"num\">4</span>开题标准</h2>\n<blockquote><p><b>一个问题值得单独追，要同时满足三件事：它的答案可能改变仓位；能在一个日期用公开材料判出落在哪一档；库里没有问题在问同一件事。</b>开多少个是判断的结果，不是目标<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6；评审 §1</span>。</p>\n<p>颗粒度按一个高端对冲基金分析员：只有会单独下注的大事开题，鸡毛蒜皮不开题（它的陈述留不留照第 5 节判）；同一个赌注的几种说法是一题，截止日、里程碑、财年和日历年各按本节\"同一题、续期，还是另一题\"里的那一条判<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</p>\n<p>另有一条前提：新问题要有独立的投资判断；一个新产品、一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开<span class=\"src\">D201</span>。</p></blockquote>\n\n<h3>四个测试<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6</span></h3>\n<ol class=\"steps\">\n<li><b>值得追</b>写得出\"这个结果会改变哪项收入、利润、现金或信用风险、竞争位置\"吗？写不出就留作证据，不开题。\"数字很大\"不算理由。单笔交易、产品、项目，规模够不上改变公司的收入、利润、现金或信用风险的，不开题，陈述留不留照第 5 节判<span class=\"src\">D248 第 6 条：问的就是小交易、小产品</span>；这一测试的其余理由（包括竞争位置）不变。</li>\n<li><b>独立意义</b>能写出两个情景吗：其他问题的答案不变，只有这一题相反，而对业务的判断确实不同？写不出就优先作为证据<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 3、8 条</span>。评审里的一个判例：NVIDIA FY2027 总收入题判为数据中心收入题的证据，理由是\"该段明确说主要增长来自数据中心，未提出独立的其他业务争论\"。这是对那一段材料的判断，别的材料要逐个判。</li>\n<li><b>能核对</b>有一个日期和一份公开材料能把答案放进事先固定的档吗？没有就重写问题。到期没有材料记\"未能判定\"，不算错。</li>\n<li><b>不是重复</b>和已有问题比，只是预测值、措辞、来源、方向或同一总量的另一种口径不同，最终核对的是同一个结果吗？是就是同一题。抽取看不到库<span class=\"src\">D211</span>，这一条在抽取时只对同一篇文章里提出的几个问题判；和库里的比由匹配做。</li>\n</ol>\n<p>另外三条写法检查<span class=\"src\">评审 §1 第 1、5、6 条</span>。没过的问题不能照原样开，要重写；重写不了就不开，材料作证据。</p>\n<ul>\n<li><b>原文支持：</b>主体、量或事件、时间依据都能在原文找到。原文没给日期、而规则允许研究员定检查日的，用那个日期并标明：没写日期的待决监管事项用本财年末（第 3 节 E 类）；还没签的约束性义务用文章后 18 个月以内能核对签约的那天<span class=\"src\">D185、D210</span>。不把\"拟议\"\"预计\"写成\"已签\"\"已完成\"。</li>\n<li><b>口径完整：</b>算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚；支出、融资、担保、订单、收入不混。</li>\n<li><b>时间正确：</b>原文支持这个期间，不把几年的平均写成今年。</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>不开的<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 的清单</span></h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap mid\"><table>\n<thead><tr><th>不开</th><th>出处</th><th>它变成什么</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>季度数字和季度指引</td><td>第 1 版 §6；PRD 06 梯子第 6 条</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一段指引里的每一行（\"费用率、税率是模型输入，不是争论\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>没日期的\"护城河\"\"战略\"</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>高管任免、股东投票、回购授权；章程</td><td>第 1 版 §6；章程出自 D239 选定的 role-v29 原文（\"executive appointments, shareholder votes or bylaws\"）</td><td>证据或不留</td></tr>\n<tr><td>例行诉讼程序</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>客户的部署计划（\"它是供应商需求和产品问题的证据，除非改变供应商自己的现金或信用风险\"）</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据；改变公司自己的现金或信用风险时按 C 类判</td></tr>\n<tr><td>以约束性义务为理由开：公司自己借钱、自己的租约、已完成或没写规模的投资。它们不是约束性义务；对别的问题仍可以是证据，或按别的开题理由判</td><td>D236、D238</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>把远期年度预测改装成事件</td><td>第 1 版 §6</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>后年及以后的年度量（约束性义务除外）</td><td>PRD 06 梯子第 5 条；D185</td><td>证据</td></tr>\n<tr><td>同一个量的另一个估计、另一种口径、另一个来源</td><td>第 1 版 §6 测试 4</td><td>那个已开问题的证据，由匹配并入</td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n<h3>同一题、续期，还是另一题：匹配这一步的事，抽取不判库里的</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>总规则：</b>同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题；答案能分开走、而且分析员会分别下注的，才是另一题<span class=\"src\">D248</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一题：</b>同一个结果能同时判两个问题。另一个估计、来源、措辞、方向<span class=\"src\">第 1 版 §6 测试 4</span>；同一总量的另一种人群或代用口径（D190 碰撞裁决提示 collision-v1：\"another population or proxy of one aggregate\"；D197 引的 role-v12 原文：\"another population or another wording of the same aggregate is evidence to the shown aggregate thesis\"）。候选并进已开问题，用它的结果档和到期日<span class=\"src\">PRD 06</span>。只有以共同量理由开题、带量的候选由代码自动判，其余是匹配和碰撞裁决的判断。</li>\n<li><b>同一个计划的几种说法</b>（担保、融资承诺、信用支持……），最后核对的是同一个数，是一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 1 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一件事的不同截止日：</b>早的那题开着时，晚的截止日是它的证据，不另开；早的到期没有结果、事情还在追，系统开下一个截止日的续期题，带上并进来的证据，不等新文章<span class=\"src\">D248 第 2 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>同一代产品的几个里程碑：</b>一题，问能带来收入的那一步（通常是开始出货）；送样、发布作证据；会分别下注的里程碑（新药的三期数据和获批）各一题<span class=\"src\">D248 第 3 条</span>。</li>\n<li><b>公司自己的量：</b>只按财年开题；按日历年的估计是财年那题的证据，两种年份差得多时分量低一点<span class=\"src\">D248 第 4 条；PRD 06 梯子第 5 条</span>。</li>\n## D382 · 2026-11-08 · Financial figures are conditions, not theses; a thesis is a view with a reason\n\n- Alex: \"我觉得财务类型不应该是thesis，而更多的是条件。观点应该是独特的view，而不是喊出来的数字，除非有理由 - 这个理由恰恰才是观点\". On the\n  recommendation to keep a useful company figure no view takes as a condition of the company, he replied \"好\". Record:\n  `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §§16–17.\n\n## D383 · 2026-11-08 · D209 amended again: a material statement no thesis takes is kept unlinked and linked later\n\n- Alex chose \"先存着，有观点再挂\": a statement the model judges useful but no thesis takes yet is kept in the company's record, linked when\n  a related thesis opens; what the closing check rejects is still dropped, including the cash flow he ruled out. Amends D209 beyond D382.\n  Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §27.\n\n## D384 · 2026-11-08 · Clean Step 1 opens only the big matters, by the signed standard as the frozen gold applies it\n\n- Alex chose \"按金标：只开大事\": a thesis opens only for the standard's reasons (an obligation the company takes on, its main product's\n  next node, a policy step, a checkable shared quantity); another company's single project, partnership or product line is evidence.\n  The reader-based small/fragment line gives way to must_open covered and must_not not opened. Class A (main-driver quantity) stays\n  out under D382. Record: `clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md` §36.\n\n## D385 · 2026-11-08 · Target prices and valuation conclusions are not kept\n## D490 · 2026-11-14 · Alex opens a test: the new system may open questions on the company's revenue and margin\n\n- **Asked** (after D489, his reply to this exact question): \"这一周的对比显示：现行系统会为营收、毛利率开问题；新系统按你之前定的规则（D382：财务数字是条件，不是\n  问题）不开，所以两组盲评读者都列出的 5 件大事里它少了 3 件（FY2027 营收、FY2028 营收、FY2028 毛利率），145 条公司财务数字没有被任何判断读到。新系统接下来怎么处理营收\n  和毛利率？\" Options: test opening such questions (recommended); keep the rule; open none but use the figures.\n- **Alex:** \"试开这类问题 (Recommended)\". The option as shown to him: \"先在这周已存的文章上花几美分试：能否开出这 3 个问题，同时不乱开、不重复；通过后再跑第二个没用过的\n  新鲜周。会改变你的 D382/D384。历史上类似的放开曾多开 7 个不该开的问题（那次同时改了三处）。\"\n- **Decided:** a test arm of clean Step 1 is opened (a new version of the frozen c8 request, for this test only; c8 stays the adopted\n  request until a result is adopted). D382 and D384 stay in force for the adopted path; the arm departs from them on one point, the\n  company's main numbers as questions. First a probe of a few cents on the stored week's states, with its lines and stop condition written\n  before any send and a council round before the send (AGENTS §7.3); the second fresh week runs only if the probe meets its lines.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"**Version 2 fixes the broad scope, the growth example, and the instruction to name measure and scope. The missing-date issue is only partly fixed.** The request now says to use the annual results release, but if the article gives no release date, it still gives the model no supported calendar date to put in the answer.\n\nFor example, an article may forecast next year’s revenue without saying when the company will publish it. “The release of that fiscal year’s results” identifies the event, but does not establish its date. The model could return an unspecific event, invent a date, or decline to open the question.\n\nThis is a **read-only assessment of the text**, not a measurement of model behavior. I ran diffs on the system and closing texts and compared the schemas as parsed JSON. The schema adds `main_driver` to the allowed reasons and changes “four” to “five”; there are no other parsed schema changes.\n\nThe deliberate restriction to revenue and gross margin is documented in [PROBE-DESIGN.md](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/PROBE-DESIGN.md) and authorized for this test by [D490](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:5571). It is narrower than the signed standard’s full row A, but that narrowing is **not a finding**.\n\n### Version 1 findings\n\n| Earlier point | Version 2 assessment |\n|---|---|\n| Scope extended beyond revenue and margin | **Resolved for the test.** The new opening words say “the company’s own annual revenue or gross margin”; the fuel-cost example is gone. The two remaining examples still need clearer scope, discussed below. |\n| No date when the item gives none | **Partly addressed, still unresolved.** The date rule now names the results release. It does not supply a date or explain what to do when that release date is unknown. |\n| Growth example could invite a duplicate | **Improved.** “Same-store sales growth” is now “same-store sales,” and the text says level and growth are one question when the same reported figure settles both. The wider comparison between two new questions can still be clearer. |\n| Measure and scope were not explicitly requested | **Addressed in the instruction.** “Name the measure, its scope and the fiscal year” is now explicit. The examples do not show the full scope, and the request does not explicitly say the fiscal year must be supported by the item. |\n\nSources for the prior points and revision: [version 1 audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/main-numbers/audit-c20-blind.md), [candidate system](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-system.txt:87), and [candidate schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json:30).\n\n### Each changed sentence\n\nThe standard references below are [§3 and §4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html:272). D382 says financial figures are conditions unless the reason itself is a view; D384 excluded row A from the adopted clean request. D490 opens this departure **as a test**, while those decisions remain in force for the adopted path. [D382 and D384](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4107)\n\n| Changed text | Verdict | Source and assessment |\n|---|---|---|\n| “It opens for one of **five reasons**, a closed set” | **Consistent**, for this test. | §3: “开题理由是封闭的” and lists five categories. D490 permits testing the addition; it does not adopt it. |\n| “`main_driver`: the company’s own annual revenue or gross margin, for its current or next fiscal year, whether or not the company guides it …” | **Keeps narrower**, deliberately. | Row A: “承载公司价值的那个年度量，不管公司指不指引” and “公司财年的今年或明年.” The standard also permits other main annual quantities; D490 limits this test. A possible ambiguity remains: “the revenue that carries the business” grammatically qualifies revenue more clearly than it qualifies gross margin, while row A requires the main value-carrying quantity. |\n| “… the revenue that carries the business, in total or of its main segment, or the gross margin” | **Consistent**, subject to the separate-question test. | Row A names “撑起业务的分部收入、毛利率.” §4 says “一个新数字、一个更窄的范围，单凭这些不开.” A main segment is eligible, but its existence alone does not justify a second question beside total revenue. |\n| “the bank’s net interest income this fiscal year”; “the retailer’s same-store sales next fiscal year” | **Consistent in substance**, but underspecified as complete questions. | Both measures appear in row A: “银行的净利息收入、零售商的同店销售.” Neither example states the reporting scope needed to distinguish, for example, total sales from a comparable-store measure. Whether each is treated as revenue within this narrower test can be made clearer. |\n| “It is not every line of the statements.” | **Consistent.** | Row A: “不是每一行报表数.” |\n| “Name the measure, its scope and the fiscal year” | **Consistent.** | §4: “算谁、不算谁、算什么写清楚” and “原文支持这个期间.” The sentence asks for the year but does not repeat that it must be supported. |\n| “A level and its growth rate are one thesis when the same reported figure settles both.” | **Consistent.** | §4: “同一个结果能判掉两题，就是同一题.” The condition matters: a growth question also needs its comparison period and measure identified before one can establish what settles it. |\n| “The material that publishes the figure, usually the annual report, settles it.” | **Consistent.** | Row A: “公布这个数的公开材料，通常是年报.” The actual material must publish the specified measure and scope. |\n| When the item gives no date, use “a `main_driver` quantity, the release of that fiscal year’s results” | **No source for treating an unknown release event as an available calendar date.** The choice of release as the due date is **consistent**. | Row A says “到期日是这个数的发布日.” But §4 requires “有一个日期和一份公开材料” and requires the time basis in the source. Its explicit analyst-set dates are for an undated pending regulatory decision and an unsigned obligation. It does not grant an arbitrary date for an annual quantity. |\n| Do not open “a quarter’s figures or guidance, or the level, growth, margin or guidance of a financial measure that is not a `main_driver` quantity, on its own” | **Consistent with the test’s exception, with an ambiguity affecting other reasons.** | §4 excludes “季度数字和季度指引” and every line of guidance; row A permits a qualifying annual main driver. “On its own” preserves other reasons in principle, but a reader could apply the financial-measure exclusion to a separately qualifying obligation or shared quantity. |\n| Closing check: “five reasons” | **Consistent**, conditional on the fifth reason being applied correctly. | §3’s reasons are a closed set; the rest of the check still requires public material, a date and compliance with the exclusions. |\n| Schema enum adds `main_driver`; description changes to “one of the five” | **Consistent.** | Row A uses `main_driver`; D490 opens the test. The schema can represent the new reason, but the enum does not enforce its measure, scope or date. |\n\n### Other sentences in the request\n\n- **Role paragraph:** No direct contradiction. It says new questions must be important, raised by the item and supported by evidence, and “Never open a thesis only to give a statement a home.” The new reason still sits under those conditions. A bare figure should not automatically become a question just because the new reason exists.\n\n- **CONDITION:** No direct contradiction. “Inform an open thesis about its revenue or earnings path” describes where figures can link; the next sentence expressly recognizes “open or new” questions. A figure may support a newly proposed annual question. The wording could nevertheless pull toward linking only to an already open question if the model gives the first sentence too much weight.\n\n- **“One quantity for one period, or one event”:** Compatible with annual revenue or gross margin. It does not itself tell the model whether two differently worded questions describe the same result.\n\n- **Date rule:** The new fallback conflicts in practice with “Give the date the item supports” when the item does not give the results-release date. The instruction names *what date to use*, but does not make that date known. The schema’s `period` accepts a string or null and asks for the period **or** check date “with how it was set”; `settled_by` asks for material that settles the answer “on a date.” Neither supplies an actual date. [Schema](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/arms/c20-schema.json:38)\n\n- **Another estimate, source or wording:** Compatible. A later forecast for the same question should be evidence for it. The new level-and-growth sentence improves this boundary, though it does not explicitly walk the total-versus-segment comparison.\n\n- **“An annual quantity after next year”:** Compatible with current or next **fiscal** year. The model must use the company’s fiscal year rather than silently treating calendar years as fiscal years.\n\n- **`closest_open_thesis` and `why_a_separate_bet`:** Compatible for comparison with an existing question: the model must explain how their answers can move apart. These fields do not ask for that comparison against another question proposed in the same answer. The closing check compares new questions for “the same underlying question,” but its explicit “cannot move apart” test mentions only an open question.\n\n- **Closing check, figures and conditions:** The instruction not to drop a retold figure, guidance or forecast concerns keeping evidence; it does not make each figure a new question. The sentence that a missing date does not drop an **evidence item** is also compatible with requiring a date to open a **question**. The same-fact row combines a reported measure and its growth rates in one evidence item; the new level-and-growth sentence concerns questions. Finally, the extra usefulness check for the company’s figures applies to statements returned **without links**. A statement linked to a new question still faces the general evidence test, but no longer faces that particular unlinked-figure check.\n\n- **Closing check, reasons:** “Five reasons” preserves all four existing reasons. There is no explicit instruction to replace or suppress them.\n\n### Examples\n\nThe two added examples use generic bank and retailer descriptions. They name no covered company, product, or numerical value, and row A supports both measures. They are cross-industry examples, though the eligibility principle should still apply in any industry.\n\nThey fit the schema as **partial illustrations**, not complete valid questions: neither specifies the full scope, a public source that will publish that exact measure, or an actual settlement date. “Same-store sales” also describes a subset or comparable-store measure, so calling it simply the company’s revenue could blur the scope. The model needs to name that distinction when it matters.\n\n### Specific risks and smallest sourced clarifications\n\n**a. Every statement line, including EPS, net income, cash flow or a small segment.** The words most likely to cause over-opening are “the company’s own annual revenue or gross margin” if read as sufficient by itself, and “or the gross margin,” which is less clearly tied to the value-carrying test than revenue is. The surrounding “not every line,” position-impact and separate-bet tests oppose indiscriminate opening. EPS, net income and cash flow are outside the new reason as written; a small segment fails unless it is the qualifying main segment and separately significant.\n\nA small clarification is: **“the revenue or gross margin that carries the company’s value”**, retaining “in total or of its main segment” where applicable. This carries row A’s own importance boundary to both measures.\n\n**b. A quarter or a year after next fiscal year.** “Annual,” “current or next fiscal year,” the quarter exclusion and the later-year exclusion already oppose both. No new prohibition is needed. The remaining gap is source support: add **“Use a fiscal year supported by the item”**, reflecting §4’s “原文支持这个期间.” A quarterly statement may inform an annual question; it should not be converted into an unsupported annual forecast.\n\n**c. Two questions for level and growth, or total and main segment.** The new “same reported figure” sentence addresses level and growth. The words “in total or of its main segment,” together with a comparison that explicitly asks whether answers move apart only against an **open** question, leave a risk of two unnecessary new questions. Total and segment must not be automatically merged: §4 says to judge whether their answers can move apart and matter independently on the actual material.\n\nThe smallest general clarification is: **“Compare new questions with each other as well: if the same result settles both, keep one; separate them only when their answers can move apart and an analyst would bet on them separately.”** This follows §4’s same-result and independent-meaning tests.\n\n**d. Another company’s figures.** “The company” is defined as `current_entity`, and the new reason says “the company’s own,” so another company’s figure does not qualify under this reason. Other-party evidence can still inform research on the company. No extra rule is needed for this test. The signed standard separately discusses proposing another company’s own question, so this conclusion should not be generalized beyond the current request’s company scope.\n\n**e. The other four reasons stop opening.** The five reasons remain alternatives, but “a quarter’s figures or guidance, or … a financial measure that is not a `main_driver` quantity” could be overread as blocking a quantity that independently qualifies as an obligation or a shared quantity. A minimal clarification is: **“This row does not exclude a matter that independently meets another opening reason.”** That preserves the existing reasons; it does not make a financial line sufficient by itself.\n\n### What is still needed to write the question\n\n- **Measure and scope:** Now requested explicitly. The answer must say what is counted—for example, total revenue or a named main segment, and the exact gross-margin measure. The illustrations do not demonstrate that full scope.\n- **Fiscal year:** Requested explicitly, but the item must support the chosen year. The request should say so rather than invite a guess.\n- **Settling material:** Present: the public material that publishes the specified figure, usually the annual report. The answer must identify material capable of resolving the actual measure and scope.\n- **Date:** **Still missing when the source does not provide the release date.** The revision identifies the release as the relevant event, but neither the request nor the schema supplies its calendar date. The signed standard requires a date and does not give this category an analyst-set fallback. The text alone therefore cannot resolve this case without either a supported date from an available input or a separately decided way to handle its absence."}}
